WEBVTT

00:31.732 --> 00:33.599
Sir, one minute warning.

00:33.734 --> 00:34.990
Congratulations again.

00:35.126 --> 00:37.398
Heard anything from
Betty, from my daughter?

00:37.533 --> 00:39.635
No, sir. We tried
her several times.

00:39.770 --> 00:40.770
Okay.

00:40.904 --> 00:42.404
Thank you.

00:43.705 --> 00:45.874
All
right, New Hampshire,

00:46.010 --> 00:47.974
we are moments away.

00:48.110 --> 00:50.377
Are you ready?

00:50.513 --> 00:53.214
Ready for
Ross! Ready for Ross!

00:53.349 --> 00:56.316
Ready for Ross!
Ready for Ross!

00:56.451 --> 00:59.453
Ready for Ross!
Ready for Ross!

00:59.589 --> 01:01.293
Ladies and gentlemen,

01:01.428 --> 01:05.596
the next President of the
United States of America,

01:05.732 --> 01:07.863
Thaddeus Ross!

01:28.149 --> 01:29.583
Thank you.

01:31.122 --> 01:34.821
Tonight, America has spoken

01:34.957 --> 01:39.824
in one of the most important
elections of our lifetimes.

01:39.959 --> 01:43.935
We've recognized the
urgency of this moment.

01:44.271 --> 01:48.370
From the disappearance
of half of mankind

01:48.505 --> 01:51.533
to the emergence
of a celestial mass

01:51.669 --> 01:53.344
in the Indian Ocean,

01:53.480 --> 01:57.678
the threats we face show
no signs of slowing down.

01:57.813 --> 02:03.716
But the only way we can
overcome them is together!

02:04.451 --> 02:05.782
Tonight, President Ross

02:05.918 --> 02:07.583
embraced the theme
of togetherness

02:07.719 --> 02:08.950
in his acceptance speech,

02:09.086 --> 02:11.186
but his past tells
a different story,

02:11.321 --> 02:13.161
especially when it comes
to working with heroes

02:13.229 --> 02:14.594
like Captain America.

02:14.730 --> 02:17.035
As two of our nation's
most important leaders,

02:17.171 --> 02:19.070
some question if
they can overcome

02:19.206 --> 02:21.433
their at-times
tumultuous history

02:21.569 --> 02:23.303
to face the challenges ahead.

02:23.439 --> 02:25.004
Here you go, Cap.

02:25.139 --> 02:26.718
During his
time as a four-star general...

02:26.742 --> 02:28.712
Put your money away.
It's on the house.

02:30.079 --> 02:31.215
Thanks, Charlie.

02:31.350 --> 02:32.813
...leading to Ross

02:32.948 --> 02:35.383
being branded with the
moniker of "the Hulk Hunter."

02:35.519 --> 02:37.217
Following Hulk and
the Abomination's

02:37.352 --> 02:38.619
destruction of Harlem,

02:38.754 --> 02:40.755
Ross was criticized
for what some called

02:40.890 --> 02:44.326
"an unwarranted outburst"
during a press conference.

02:44.828 --> 02:47.726
In fact, many blamed Ross
for the collateral damage,

02:47.862 --> 02:49.628
believing it was his
relentless pursuit

02:49.764 --> 02:52.435
of Banner's Hulk that
led to the rampage.

02:52.570 --> 02:54.831
It also resulted in
the President-elect's

02:54.967 --> 02:56.340
estrangement from his daughter,

02:56.475 --> 02:59.935
Dr. Betty Ross, Bruce
Banner's ex-girlfriend.

03:00.070 --> 03:01.442
But in a surprising
turn of events,

03:01.578 --> 03:03.081
he managed to shift
the narrative,

03:03.217 --> 03:05.050
and silence his harshest critics

03:05.186 --> 03:07.147
by apprehending
the man responsible

03:07.283 --> 03:08.718
for the Abomination.

03:37.809 --> 03:39.015
How we lookin' down there?

03:39.151 --> 03:40.383
Well, SERPENT mercenaries

03:40.519 --> 03:42.199
entered with the package
about an hour ago.

03:42.279 --> 03:44.118
They're handing it to
the buyer any minute.

03:44.487 --> 03:45.718
We know what they're carrying?

03:45.854 --> 03:47.649
That is classified
per the White House.

03:47.785 --> 03:49.460
Of course it is.

03:49.595 --> 03:51.527
Where's Eagle-One? We
have strike authorization.

03:51.662 --> 03:54.656
Eagle-One is entering
the target airspace now.

03:58.163 --> 04:00.071
Upload the compound's
covert entry points.

04:00.206 --> 04:03.132
Covert? Really?
You must be new.

04:14.612 --> 04:15.650
Wait for it.

04:32.701 --> 04:34.104
Sam, SEAL team is
six minutes out.

04:34.239 --> 04:35.406
Copy that.

04:53.118 --> 04:54.557
How the hell did
he just do that?

04:54.692 --> 04:56.257
Cap's gear was a gift
from the Wakandans

04:56.392 --> 04:57.826
for helping them out.

04:57.962 --> 05:00.464
I heard even the wrapping
paper was made of vibranium.

05:01.828 --> 05:04.369
No, man. I'm kidding. Come on.

05:07.739 --> 05:10.735
Joaquin, Redwing's pickin'
up hostages inside.

05:10.870 --> 05:12.274
- I'm goin' in.
- Negative.

05:12.409 --> 05:13.941
The package is the priority.

05:14.077 --> 05:15.288
Have the
SEALs track down the package.

05:15.312 --> 05:17.074
I'm on the hostages.

05:18.177 --> 05:20.551
Redwing, send them a
scan of the building.

05:22.020 --> 05:23.278
What is it?

05:23.414 --> 05:25.134
That's Sidewinder. He's
the head of SERPENT.

05:25.159 --> 05:27.216
He's not supposed to be here.

05:34.933 --> 05:36.264
Ah.

05:36.399 --> 05:38.595
You're praying, Padre.

05:45.309 --> 05:46.476
Padre.

05:52.416 --> 05:55.983
Padre. Padre, Padre, Padre.

06:11.302 --> 06:12.401
Kill them.

06:12.804 --> 06:14.806
- No. No!
- Kill them one at a time.

06:16.701 --> 06:17.938
Silencio!

06:18.074 --> 06:18.810
Captain America is here.

06:18.945 --> 06:19.636
Do you copy?

06:19.771 --> 06:21.440
Move, move, move!

06:21.575 --> 06:24.042
Vámonos, vámonos.

06:25.812 --> 06:27.584
Get the package outta here.

06:58.750 --> 07:00.510
SERPENT's on the move
with the canister, Sam.

07:00.544 --> 07:02.586
I'm
kinda busy right now!

07:29.347 --> 07:31.714
Redwing, on my mark.

07:34.847 --> 07:36.081
Stop.

07:37.589 --> 07:39.714
Stay back! Or
we'll shoot them.

07:54.500 --> 07:56.620
SERPENT's gettin' farther
away with the canister, Sam,

07:56.709 --> 07:58.543
and Sidewinder's
headed to the chapel.

07:59.546 --> 08:01.106
I already know what
you're trying to do.

08:01.173 --> 08:03.174
You can't be at
two places at once.

08:04.041 --> 08:05.282
All right, this time.

08:05.418 --> 08:06.743
But don't get yourself killed.

08:06.879 --> 08:08.047
No dying. Copy that.

08:17.955 --> 08:19.364
Buyer didn't show.

08:19.500 --> 08:21.065
Looks like you need
better clients.

08:21.201 --> 08:22.895
You don't need to worry.

08:23.030 --> 08:25.059
I'll find whoever
wasted my time.

08:25.195 --> 08:26.866
You have bigger concerns.

08:52.457 --> 08:54.197
The Captain America
I dreamt of killing

08:54.333 --> 08:55.333
was bigger than you.

08:55.400 --> 08:57.393
I'm happy to disappoint.

09:00.471 --> 09:02.541
I bet you break easy.

09:03.110 --> 09:04.433
Not that easy.

09:17.080 --> 09:18.122
Not that hard.

09:18.258 --> 09:19.948
I heard your rib go.

09:20.083 --> 09:21.385
You need a minute?

09:21.520 --> 09:23.206
Nope. Nope,
let's get this over with.

09:23.230 --> 09:25.322
I got shit to do today.

09:40.608 --> 09:42.581
Whoo-hoo!

09:44.677 --> 09:45.677
Damn.

09:45.745 --> 09:47.278
Nobody saw that.

09:48.915 --> 09:51.084
Sam, package is secured.

09:57.422 --> 09:59.598
I'll add your star
to my collection.

10:09.869 --> 10:11.108
Need a minute?

10:15.876 --> 10:17.176
That's what I thought.

10:32.057 --> 10:33.623
Save some for us, Cap.

10:34.426 --> 10:36.628
He has a fractured
arm, so be gentle.

10:43.909 --> 10:46.500
"Keep your face
always to the sunshine,

10:46.636 --> 10:48.940
and the shadows will
fall behind you."

10:49.075 --> 10:51.373
The quote was Betty's idea.

10:51.508 --> 10:53.577
She's still not
speaking with you?

10:53.713 --> 10:54.882
No.

10:55.018 --> 10:57.217
She doesn't believe
I've changed.

10:57.586 --> 10:59.251
Really changed.

11:01.223 --> 11:03.522
I don't think I'm
gonna get another shot.

11:04.492 --> 11:07.424
Comin' up on the end of my
first hundred days, Leila.

11:08.863 --> 11:10.493
They're gonna define me.

11:12.131 --> 11:14.233
This treaty's gotta work.

11:18.936 --> 11:20.339
Hello.

11:20.474 --> 11:22.316
Mr. President,
the mission was a success.

11:22.340 --> 11:23.604
All right, fill me in.

11:23.940 --> 11:26.245
Cap and the SEAL
team saved the hostages.

11:26.380 --> 11:29.177
The package is secure
and en route to the US.

11:29.647 --> 11:30.927
How's your brother?

11:30.951 --> 11:32.313
Oh, wow, you remembered.

11:32.449 --> 11:34.056
- He's in the Air Force.
- Yeah?

11:34.192 --> 11:36.232
Probably 'cause of you.

11:36.290 --> 11:38.020
I try not to hold
that against him.

11:38.155 --> 11:39.189
It's a weird place

11:39.324 --> 11:40.760
- for a handoff, right?
- Mm-hmm.

11:40.896 --> 11:42.797
Wide open, soft perimeter.

11:43.332 --> 11:45.359
You think the buyer ever
intended on showin' up?

11:45.495 --> 11:46.964
You think SERPENT got played?

11:47.099 --> 11:48.298
What are they sayin'?

11:48.434 --> 11:50.303
Same thing. Contract
was anonymous.

11:50.438 --> 11:53.469
Fifty mil to steal the
canister en route to Japan.

11:53.605 --> 11:55.574
Then show up here
and meet the buyer.

11:55.943 --> 11:57.144
Hmm.

11:58.842 --> 12:01.750
Let us know if you get
a trace on Sidewinder.

12:01.885 --> 12:03.447
- Good work.
- Thank you.

12:07.858 --> 12:10.388
You'll notice, I did not die,

12:10.523 --> 12:12.692
and people are saying
I did not die in style.

12:12.828 --> 12:13.924
Who is saying that?

12:14.293 --> 12:15.357
- People.
- What people?

12:15.492 --> 12:16.598
Everybody.

12:16.734 --> 12:18.165
Everybody is saying that.

12:18.567 --> 12:21.002
Look, tell me I don't make
your old gear look brand-new.

12:21.138 --> 12:23.603
You've got on the
greaves upside down.

12:23.738 --> 12:24.869
I'm joking.

12:25.005 --> 12:26.310
You look good, man.

12:26.446 --> 12:27.873
All right. Fair enough.

12:28.243 --> 12:29.249
That means that
you're finally gonna

12:29.273 --> 12:30.345
introduce me to Ant-Man?

12:30.480 --> 12:31.609
Nope.

12:32.412 --> 12:33.692
Well, at least
you gotta teach me

12:33.717 --> 12:35.151
your aerial kick, man.

12:35.287 --> 12:37.919
Look, if I'm gonna be Falcon,
I gotta know everything.

12:38.054 --> 12:39.616
In no way are you
ready for that.

12:39.751 --> 12:41.754
But I got a guy who'll
teach you the fundamentals

12:41.890 --> 12:42.890
from the ground up.

12:42.922 --> 12:43.922
Absolutely.

12:44.026 --> 12:45.622
Now, he's not a people person.

12:45.757 --> 12:47.726
So you gotta learn how
to keep your mouth shut.

12:47.861 --> 12:49.163
Can you do that?

12:51.564 --> 12:53.284
He's gonna love me,
bro! Are you kidding me?

12:53.337 --> 12:55.377
- That's not the right answer.
- He's gonna love me.

13:02.613 --> 13:03.348
What's up, OG?

13:03.483 --> 13:04.739
Who's the pretty boy?

13:04.874 --> 13:06.674
"Pretty boy"? You didn't
tell gramps about me?

13:06.783 --> 13:07.783
I'm the new Falcon.

13:07.918 --> 13:09.276
- No, you're not.
- Yes, I am.

13:09.412 --> 13:11.184
This is Joaquin Torres.

13:11.320 --> 13:12.824
Been workin' with
him for three years.

13:12.959 --> 13:14.719
I haven't figured out
how to shut him up yet.

13:14.852 --> 13:17.320
So what are we doing
here? Orthopedics? Uh...

13:17.822 --> 13:20.590
How to relearn how to walk
after you break a hip?

13:23.731 --> 13:25.100
Oh, sh...

13:26.570 --> 13:27.802
Oh, shit.

13:27.937 --> 13:29.165
That's Isaiah Bradley.

13:29.301 --> 13:31.673
The... The Isaiah Bradley?

13:32.175 --> 13:33.709
You brought me to
the forgotten Cap?

13:33.845 --> 13:34.921
Why didn't you say something?

13:34.945 --> 13:36.605
It is a pleasure to meet you.

13:36.740 --> 13:39.311
Your missions in
Korea are legendary.

13:39.446 --> 13:40.949
And what, and after
that, no action?

13:41.085 --> 13:42.425
I mean, a lot's
changed in the world.

13:42.449 --> 13:43.969
We could've used
another super soldier.

13:44.019 --> 13:45.151
The United States government

13:45.287 --> 13:47.318
threw me in prison for 30 years.

13:47.454 --> 13:50.721
They experimented
on me for decades.

13:51.257 --> 13:52.956
Yikes, that's... that sucks.

13:53.092 --> 13:54.397
Can we start?

13:54.532 --> 13:55.124
Let's do it.

13:55.260 --> 13:57.165
No vibranium wings,

13:58.068 --> 14:01.367
no shield, no super
soldier serum.

14:02.701 --> 14:05.039
I wanna see if he's
got three in him.

14:05.175 --> 14:07.005
Get
those flags, Sam!

14:08.106 --> 14:09.540
Cap v Cap!

14:15.719 --> 14:16.719
That's one.

14:17.720 --> 14:18.915
Let's go!

14:19.451 --> 14:21.057
Orthopedic.

14:25.563 --> 14:26.658
That's two.

14:33.731 --> 14:36.472
I'm sorry. What
were you sayin'?

14:36.841 --> 14:38.539
See? Not a people person.

14:38.674 --> 14:41.810
- In a fight, the last hit...
- Is the only hit that matters.

14:41.945 --> 14:43.442
I know. Shut up, but thanks.

14:43.578 --> 14:45.577
All right, that's it.
Tag me in. I'm ready.

14:45.712 --> 14:49.217
Captain America doesn't
get to take five. Let's go.

14:49.952 --> 14:51.582
I need to take this.

14:52.251 --> 14:53.749
I'm not takin' five.

14:56.986 --> 15:00.063
- You still got the plastic on.
- No! I don't...

15:01.294 --> 15:03.091
Maybe I wanted it on there.

15:03.794 --> 15:05.634
Oh, you want me to
make the text bigger?

15:05.770 --> 15:07.167
So you can read it?

15:07.302 --> 15:09.237
Yeah, I'll hold
for the President.

15:17.681 --> 15:19.016
Where you going?

15:21.984 --> 15:23.284
You wanna talk about it?

15:26.651 --> 15:30.192
It just doesn't
sit right with me.

15:30.328 --> 15:33.691
Captain America, answering
to the President.

15:33.826 --> 15:36.599
The President of the
country who stole your life?

15:36.735 --> 15:38.135
It's not just that.

15:38.270 --> 15:41.401
We're talkin' about
Thaddeus "Thunderbolt" Ross.

15:41.536 --> 15:43.368
Son of a bitch earned
that nickname, too.

15:43.504 --> 15:45.536
Look, I know, Isaiah, firsthand.

15:45.671 --> 15:48.177
Remember, Ross threw
me in the Raft.

15:48.312 --> 15:50.506
Hounded me, Steve and
Natasha for years.

15:50.641 --> 15:51.941
So why are you workin' for him?

15:53.014 --> 15:54.348
As long as you do,

15:54.483 --> 15:57.451
Captain America stands
for people like him.

15:57.586 --> 16:00.088
You've got no business
workin' for the government.

16:00.223 --> 16:02.192
You see what's
going on out there?

16:02.728 --> 16:04.594
The country is lost.

16:05.029 --> 16:06.596
Standing next to the President,

16:06.732 --> 16:08.164
even if it's Ross...

16:08.866 --> 16:10.630
it gives people hope.

16:11.466 --> 16:13.104
Now, come on, give
me some credit.

16:13.239 --> 16:14.999
I have a friend who
works in the White House.

16:15.066 --> 16:18.372
She'll let me know if Ross
starts acting out of turn.

16:20.212 --> 16:22.541
None of this means
I forgot about you.

16:23.881 --> 16:25.382
I see what you're doin'.

16:25.517 --> 16:26.576
What?

16:26.712 --> 16:28.417
Pullin' that counseling
bullshit on me.

16:30.688 --> 16:31.688
Look, trust me.

16:31.816 --> 16:34.021
My eyes are wide
open on this, okay?

16:34.157 --> 16:37.226
I know Ross will never change,

16:38.225 --> 16:40.329
but he is the President.

16:41.232 --> 16:42.506
So you gonna tell
me what he wanted

16:42.530 --> 16:44.530
or are you plannin'
on makin' me guess?

16:45.831 --> 16:48.268
He invited Joaquin and
I to the White House,

16:48.403 --> 16:50.633
and I said under one condition.

16:50.935 --> 16:53.671
If he extended an
invitation to you as well.

16:54.572 --> 16:56.072
I know you're gonna say no,

16:57.008 --> 16:59.413
but it would mean a lot
to me if you were there.

17:00.347 --> 17:01.813
We just...

17:02.216 --> 17:03.884
...gotta get you a suit.

17:04.020 --> 17:05.621
I have a damn suit.

17:05.756 --> 17:07.055
For real?

17:07.190 --> 17:08.298
Then why are you always wearin'

17:08.322 --> 17:10.226
that ratty-ass sweatsuit?

17:12.064 --> 17:14.065
Come on, you gonna come or what?

17:20.966 --> 17:22.747
See, Isaiah? This
is what I'm talking about.

17:22.771 --> 17:25.406
Now you're going to the
White House. Look at that.

17:25.541 --> 17:27.181
- You look good, OG.
- Wow, man.

17:27.303 --> 17:28.823
I told you I was gonna get
you out of those sweats.

17:28.847 --> 17:30.279
Look at you now, man.

17:30.414 --> 17:32.778
I didn't know Men's
Warehouse made that size.

17:34.252 --> 17:36.352
Hey, Faith and I
got married in this.

17:36.487 --> 17:38.229
Okay, all right, all right.

17:38.253 --> 17:39.380
I'm sure she would be proud.

17:39.515 --> 17:40.820
I hope so.

17:41.890 --> 17:44.929
Feels strange to walk right
into the belly of the beast.

17:45.065 --> 17:46.305
Hey, I'm sure it can't be easy.

17:46.391 --> 17:47.525
It ain't.

17:47.661 --> 17:48.999
Which is why we gotta celebrate.

17:49.135 --> 17:50.761
I don't care if it
is Ross in charge.

17:50.896 --> 17:52.796
We are guests of honor
at the White House, man!

17:52.931 --> 17:54.510
- When does that ever happen?
- Right.

17:54.534 --> 17:56.000
And they sent us a limo, man.

17:56.135 --> 17:57.432
What?

17:57.567 --> 17:59.041
And we look good.

17:59.176 --> 18:00.441
- Yeah.
- What?

18:00.576 --> 18:02.096
Old school, you got
your smell-good on.

18:02.178 --> 18:03.310
What?

18:03.446 --> 18:05.239
And you got the houndstooth on.

18:05.742 --> 18:07.542
And we got the good stuff.

18:07.678 --> 18:09.720
It's party time.

18:20.230 --> 18:21.510
Captain America!

18:21.630 --> 18:23.398
Captain,
Captain, over here.

18:23.533 --> 18:25.902
- Cap, over here!
- Mr. Bradley.

18:26.037 --> 18:27.169
Over here!

18:27.305 --> 18:28.625
- Hey, Isaiah. Check it out.
- Oh.

18:36.277 --> 18:40.283
Whoa, man, look at this!

18:42.085 --> 18:43.785
Oh, we gotta get a pic.

18:43.920 --> 18:45.156
Let's do it.

18:46.991 --> 18:48.252
Tres amigos on three.

18:48.388 --> 18:50.495
Uno, dos, tres. Ah!

18:52.499 --> 18:54.308
Yeah, that's my
new wallpaper. Look at that.

18:54.332 --> 18:55.472
- Pretty good.
- It's good?

18:55.496 --> 18:56.727
Can you
send it to me?

18:56.863 --> 18:58.378
Yeah, I'll AirDrop
it to you right now.

18:58.402 --> 18:59.927
You do know what
AirDrop is, right?

19:00.062 --> 19:02.004
Of course, I know
what AirDrop is.

19:02.140 --> 19:04.003
What's AirDrop?

19:04.405 --> 19:05.525
You see, you should have it.

19:05.639 --> 19:07.167
Just hit "Accept"
and it pops up.

19:07.303 --> 19:09.937
- I did that.
- Excuse me, gentlemen.

19:10.073 --> 19:12.074
The President
needs Mr. Wilson.

19:12.710 --> 19:14.449
I'll see you guys inside.

19:15.382 --> 19:16.382
- Hey.
- Hey.

19:16.450 --> 19:17.855
Sam, just keep an open mind.

19:17.990 --> 19:19.619
Why? What am I walking into?

19:19.754 --> 19:22.125
Thi... This is not
the picture you took.

19:22.261 --> 19:23.686
Oh, I sent you
the wrong picture.

19:23.821 --> 19:24.861
Oh, my Lord.

19:25.397 --> 19:27.522
Well, that's
a very good point.

19:27.657 --> 19:28.694
I'll consider it.

19:29.492 --> 19:30.598
Wilson.

19:31.468 --> 19:33.501
Folks, can you give us the room?

19:35.531 --> 19:36.537
Uh...

19:38.743 --> 19:39.743
Thanks.

19:40.603 --> 19:42.002
Doctor's orders.

19:42.404 --> 19:45.440
Not quite a cigar, but
better than that damn gum.

19:45.575 --> 19:46.311
Hmm.

19:46.446 --> 19:47.674
Thanks for comin' in.

19:47.943 --> 19:49.152
Welcome to the White House.

19:49.288 --> 19:50.817
Well, thank you for
the invite, sir.

19:50.953 --> 19:54.248
I have to admit, I'm still
gettin' used to the new look.

19:54.383 --> 19:58.257
Yeah, well,
they said lose the mustache

19:58.392 --> 20:00.088
or lose the election.

20:01.696 --> 20:03.666
Thanks for your
help down in Mexico.

20:03.801 --> 20:08.070
Retrieving that canister might
just have saved this treaty.

20:08.206 --> 20:10.030
I was just doing my job, sir.

20:10.166 --> 20:11.606
You and I haven't always agreed

20:11.742 --> 20:15.803
on how much latitude
enhanced individuals deserve.

20:15.938 --> 20:17.411
But what you've accomplished

20:17.546 --> 20:19.778
has given me reason
to reconsider.

20:20.715 --> 20:24.880
Which is why I want
you, Captain America,

20:25.016 --> 20:28.325
to help me rebuild the Avengers.

20:29.425 --> 20:31.427
- The Avengers?
- Yes, sir.

20:35.466 --> 20:37.629
Well, with all due respect, sir,

20:37.765 --> 20:40.267
when you passed the
Sokovia Accords,

20:40.402 --> 20:41.772
you tore the Avengers apart.

20:41.908 --> 20:42.908
Why the change of heart?

20:42.999 --> 20:46.002
I represent all Americans now.

20:47.413 --> 20:49.979
Hell, half of 'em
wouldn't even be here

20:50.114 --> 20:51.678
without the Avengers.

20:53.117 --> 20:54.751
The country needs this.

20:55.587 --> 20:58.487
And when we disagree on how
to manage a situation...

21:00.057 --> 21:01.525
what happens then?

21:02.061 --> 21:03.426
We figure it out together.

21:05.398 --> 21:07.663
Look, you don't have to
give me an answer now.

21:08.132 --> 21:09.729
Just think about it.

21:16.041 --> 21:17.273
Prime Minister Ozaki.

21:17.408 --> 21:18.975
- Great to see you, sir.
- And you.

21:19.111 --> 21:20.509
Thank you for being here.

21:23.145 --> 21:24.313
Here we are.

21:24.449 --> 21:26.817
Sam Wilson, Prime
Minister Ozaki.

21:30.187 --> 21:31.878
Not bad.

21:32.014 --> 21:33.052
Would you like a picture?

21:33.187 --> 21:34.054
Sure.

21:34.189 --> 21:35.590
Sam, please.

21:37.463 --> 21:39.297
Stand
a little bit closer.

21:41.092 --> 21:42.562
- Thank you, gentlemen.
- Thank you.

21:42.697 --> 21:44.401
Thank you.

21:46.334 --> 21:47.562
Work with me, Sam.

21:48.331 --> 21:50.572
We'll show the world
a better way forward.

21:56.807 --> 21:58.278
That was unexpected.

21:58.414 --> 22:00.351
Maybe it's an opportunity.

22:06.088 --> 22:07.282
So?

22:07.684 --> 22:08.684
How was it?

22:08.757 --> 22:10.726
He asked me to
restart the Avengers.

22:11.395 --> 22:12.592
Wait, what now?

22:12.728 --> 22:14.596
- That's huge, man.
- I don't know.

22:15.365 --> 22:16.763
We'd have to work for him.

22:16.898 --> 22:18.535
Ladies and gentlemen,

22:18.671 --> 22:21.601
the President of the United
States, Thaddeus Ross.

22:21.737 --> 22:24.540
Good evening,
everyone. Good evening.

22:25.774 --> 22:28.412
It's my great
privilege to host you

22:28.548 --> 22:31.647
at the White House on
this historic evening.

22:31.782 --> 22:36.750
When the celestial mass
emerged in the Indian Ocean,

22:37.419 --> 22:40.089
we did what we often do.

22:40.224 --> 22:42.152
We squabbled over it.

22:42.287 --> 22:45.585
Countries rushed in to
claim it as their own,

22:45.721 --> 22:50.727
setting up research facilities
to exploit its resources.

22:52.130 --> 22:53.702
What was found
inside that island

22:53.837 --> 22:57.172
is nothing short of the
discovery of the millennium.

22:57.874 --> 23:01.705
Its potential applications
in tech, in medicine,

23:01.840 --> 23:04.674
in defense are immeasurable.

23:05.276 --> 23:09.282
It's even more indestructible
than vibranium.

23:09.985 --> 23:13.754
And it's not controlled
by an isolationist nation.

23:15.017 --> 23:16.553
Ladies and gentlemen,

23:16.689 --> 23:18.352
I present to you...

23:18.997 --> 23:20.464
adamantium.

23:24.470 --> 23:27.766
The first and only
refined sample

23:27.902 --> 23:30.467
was stolen from a
Japanese mining site.

23:30.602 --> 23:31.806
But happily,

23:31.941 --> 23:34.777
it's been recovered and
is in a secure location.

23:34.913 --> 23:39.683
And we have two incredibly
brave men to thank for that.

23:39.819 --> 23:44.752
Joaquin Torres and our own
Captain America, Sam Wilson.

23:55.699 --> 23:59.202
What we do next
with this discovery

23:59.571 --> 24:02.940
will determine how
history judges us.

24:03.242 --> 24:04.672
If we ratify this treaty,

24:04.808 --> 24:08.308
together we can produce
enough adamantium

24:08.444 --> 24:10.138
to fairly and equitably

24:10.274 --> 24:11.748
distribute it around the world.

24:13.376 --> 24:15.085
♪ I'm Mr. Blue Wa-oo-wa-oo ♪

24:15.221 --> 24:16.383
Sir, you need to sit down.

24:16.519 --> 24:18.020
♪ When you say... ♪

24:19.681 --> 24:21.987
Isaiah! What are you doing?

24:30.133 --> 24:31.359
Sam!

24:37.607 --> 24:39.075
- Sir, are you hit?
- No.

24:39.211 --> 24:41.138
Go, go, go!

25:01.828 --> 25:03.765
Mr. President, come with me.

25:35.627 --> 25:36.666
Shit.

25:51.148 --> 25:52.148
Isaiah!

26:09.426 --> 26:11.668
- Get on the ground now!
- Do not move.

26:16.208 --> 26:17.734
What's happening?

26:18.270 --> 26:20.935
I don't know. But
you gotta stop.

26:23.814 --> 26:25.616
- Stop!
- Don't!

26:29.388 --> 26:32.346
I can't go back inside, Sam.

26:32.482 --> 26:35.252
Run, and it'll be
worse than that.

26:39.021 --> 26:40.994
Please, Isaiah.

26:55.907 --> 26:57.047
Hey, take it easy!

26:57.183 --> 26:59.612
Watch my suit.

26:59.747 --> 27:03.016
Please, watch my suit.

27:16.764 --> 27:18.460
Cap, I can't let you in.

27:19.698 --> 27:20.860
Hey!

27:20.996 --> 27:22.466
Sam!

27:22.601 --> 27:25.104
Sir, you can't... you can't...

27:25.803 --> 27:26.905
Sir!

27:27.307 --> 27:29.376
- Sorry, Mr. President.
- Hey, hey, hey.

27:29.511 --> 27:30.609
He stays.

27:30.745 --> 27:32.309
Everybody else, out.

27:38.854 --> 27:40.614
Agent Taylor, you too.

27:47.090 --> 27:48.461
Are you okay?

27:49.097 --> 27:50.896
I should be asking
you that, sir.

27:51.032 --> 27:52.459
Not my first time being shot at.

27:52.595 --> 27:54.115
Look, I know how this
must look, but...

27:57.233 --> 27:58.676
Can we have a minute?

28:00.509 --> 28:01.536
She stays.

28:03.277 --> 28:07.080
Meet Ruth Bat-Seraph,
my security advisor.

28:09.614 --> 28:11.689
Sir, there's no way Isaiah
could have done this.

28:11.824 --> 28:13.720
- Except he did.
- Maybe somebody got to him.

28:13.856 --> 28:15.187
You're really defending a man

28:15.323 --> 28:17.203
who just tried to kill
the President in front...

28:17.291 --> 28:20.456
- We don't know what happened.
- Enough.

28:22.564 --> 28:23.564
What do we know?

28:23.865 --> 28:24.729
There were five shooters.

28:24.865 --> 28:26.330
Isaiah was one of them.

28:26.465 --> 28:28.464
As was Secret Service
and active military.

28:28.600 --> 28:31.370
This was a coordinated
terrorist attack, sir.

28:37.207 --> 28:38.207
What else do you have?

28:38.608 --> 28:40.045
The song that
preceded the shooting,

28:40.181 --> 28:41.621
we think it was a
cue for the attack.

28:41.744 --> 28:43.717
Sir, Isaiah looked like
he wasn't in control.

28:43.852 --> 28:45.245
He had no idea where he was.

28:45.381 --> 28:47.115
So you're suggesting what?

28:47.251 --> 28:48.552
Let me investigate.

28:50.061 --> 28:51.764
Don't you think you're a
little too close to this?

28:51.788 --> 28:53.720
Sir, your inner circle
has been compromised.

28:53.855 --> 28:56.061
There's possibility
of another attack now.

28:56.197 --> 28:57.726
And what exactly do
you have to offer

28:57.862 --> 29:00.429
that our entire intelligence
and defense apparatus can't?

29:00.565 --> 29:02.205
Well, I won't sit
around and let Isaiah...

29:02.271 --> 29:05.869
Look, I know how important
Bradley is to you.

29:06.005 --> 29:07.911
But consider the optics.

29:08.914 --> 29:12.378
Captain America conducts
a personal investigation

29:12.513 --> 29:16.183
of a friend who tried to
assassinate the President.

29:16.318 --> 29:19.213
Isaiah sacrificed
everything for this country.

29:19.349 --> 29:21.656
He's a soldier. A patriot.

29:21.791 --> 29:23.018
He had no reason to do this.

29:23.154 --> 29:24.719
He had every reason.

29:24.854 --> 29:27.222
Bradley was in prison
for rescuing his own men,

29:27.358 --> 29:29.626
experimented on for 30 years.

29:29.762 --> 29:32.665
The things done to him are
enough to make anyone snap.

29:33.235 --> 29:35.169
Sir, you invited me
here to work together.

29:35.305 --> 29:38.070
- So let's work together.
- I'm afraid that offer expired

29:38.206 --> 29:40.272
when your friend
tried to kill me.

29:44.676 --> 29:49.380
Sam, you shouldn't even
be in these situations.

29:49.983 --> 29:53.054
You're not Steve Rogers.

29:55.524 --> 29:56.785
Ruth,

29:56.920 --> 29:59.054
you have my full authority
to put this thing to bed.

29:59.823 --> 30:02.690
Before this treaty gets
compromised any further.

30:06.130 --> 30:07.365
So that's it?

30:08.604 --> 30:09.604
I'm done?

30:10.133 --> 30:11.202
You're done.

30:11.338 --> 30:13.475
This is bullshit,
and you know it.

30:13.610 --> 30:14.935
This is politics.

30:15.504 --> 30:17.705
So you better wise up, son.

30:19.916 --> 30:21.377
"Son." Who you calling "son"?

30:21.513 --> 30:23.343
Sam. What the hell
are you doing?

30:23.479 --> 30:24.679
I'm going to clear Isaiah.

30:24.814 --> 30:26.334
Storming in there
ain't gonna help him.

30:26.386 --> 30:28.551
- You need Ross on your side.
- Ross?

30:29.020 --> 30:30.155
Open your eyes.

30:30.291 --> 30:31.731
I offer to help, and
he sends me packin'.

30:31.755 --> 30:34.459
Ross is on his own side.
He always has been.

30:34.594 --> 30:36.759
Either you can't see that,
or you don't want to.

30:36.895 --> 30:38.000
Hey.

30:38.866 --> 30:39.866
Don't be that guy.

30:39.967 --> 30:41.430
And what guy is that?

30:41.566 --> 30:43.467
The one who has to
do it the hard way.

30:49.714 --> 30:51.543
Looks like I am that guy.

31:14.402 --> 31:16.535
The nation
remains on high alert.

31:16.671 --> 31:19.666
The Justice Department has
signaled a death penalty case

31:19.802 --> 31:22.676
will be pursued
against Isaiah Bradley.

31:22.812 --> 31:24.607
Just five minutes, Cap.

31:27.315 --> 31:29.617
I could be
court-martialed for this.

31:29.753 --> 31:30.848
I appreciate it, Payumo.

31:30.983 --> 31:32.219
Yes, sir.

31:58.408 --> 32:00.314
How you holdin' up?

32:00.950 --> 32:03.085
Not so good, brother Sam.

32:04.015 --> 32:05.252
Isaiah.

32:06.086 --> 32:07.353
Look me in the eye.

32:07.488 --> 32:09.283
Tell me you didn't
conspire to kill Ross.

32:09.419 --> 32:10.626
Of course I didn't.

32:10.762 --> 32:11.818
What in the world happened

32:11.953 --> 32:13.429
to make you shoot
at the President?

32:13.565 --> 32:14.657
I don't know.

32:14.792 --> 32:16.597
You gotta give me more
than "I don't know."

32:17.200 --> 32:19.300
Is there anything you remember?

32:19.702 --> 32:20.928
I got a haircut,

32:21.064 --> 32:23.633
picked my suit up at the
cleaners and came to you.

32:25.138 --> 32:27.142
We rode in the limo,

32:28.645 --> 32:30.009
took our photo.

32:30.145 --> 32:33.445
But my phone was on the fritz.

32:33.580 --> 32:37.515
And then, we went
over to the East Room.

32:38.923 --> 32:40.286
One moment I'm sittin' there,

32:40.421 --> 32:42.652
the next I'm standin'
in that park.

32:44.360 --> 32:47.024
I should have stayed
in my damn house,

32:47.160 --> 32:48.664
minded my business.

32:48.799 --> 32:49.799
No, this isn't on you.

32:49.834 --> 32:51.234
Someone's behind all this.

32:51.369 --> 32:55.533
Sam, the last thing I want
is for this to touch you.

33:03.273 --> 33:04.674
Besides...

33:09.210 --> 33:12.748
Look, there ain't no
escapin' for me this time.

33:14.418 --> 33:16.217
I'm gonna die in here.

33:16.352 --> 33:18.056
No, you're not.

33:18.191 --> 33:19.623
I'm gonna get you out.

33:24.069 --> 33:26.498
- You wanna help me?
- Of course.

33:28.672 --> 33:29.838
Don't come back.

33:35.007 --> 33:36.244
Guard.

33:53.729 --> 33:56.759
Sergeant Payumo, get me
a copy of that conversation.

33:57.935 --> 33:58.996
I wanna take another look.

33:59.131 --> 34:00.131
Yes, ma'am.

34:00.234 --> 34:02.137
And good work with Wilson.

34:02.273 --> 34:04.705
Let me know if he
pays another visit.

34:04.840 --> 34:06.076
Roger that.

34:09.010 --> 34:10.477
You get in?

34:10.612 --> 34:12.293
I think I committed
treason and espionage,

34:12.317 --> 34:15.278
but I made it into the
White House's CCTV system.

34:15.413 --> 34:16.780
What am I lookin' for?

34:16.915 --> 34:18.627
When Isaiah went
off in the White House,

34:18.651 --> 34:20.452
it made me think of
a friend of mine.

34:20.588 --> 34:22.652
He was being controlled
by trigger words.

34:22.788 --> 34:24.821
Do you see any strangers
talkin' to Isaiah?

34:24.957 --> 34:27.690
No, well, we
got there, took a picture,

34:27.826 --> 34:29.760
I AirDropped it to
him, but nothin' crazy.

34:29.895 --> 34:32.163
Yeah, but he said his
phone was on the fritz.

34:32.298 --> 34:33.298
Ah. Whoa, whoa, whoa.

34:33.433 --> 34:35.028
Sam, I think I got something.

34:36.037 --> 34:37.270
What is it?

34:37.406 --> 34:40.033
His phone is like
flashing at him.

34:42.279 --> 34:43.839
Oh, shit, I got the
same thing happening

34:43.949 --> 34:45.412
to one of the other shooters.

35:08.102 --> 35:10.239
What the hell?

35:14.308 --> 35:16.405
Warden Cooper, Ross here.

35:16.541 --> 35:18.279
The prisoner, he's secure?

35:18.415 --> 35:21.346
I can confirm the
prisoner is in his cell.

35:21.481 --> 35:23.048
Do we have eyes on the bastard?

35:23.183 --> 35:24.350
Personally.

35:24.485 --> 35:25.919
I'm looking at him
right now, sir.

35:26.054 --> 35:27.388
Thank you, Cooper.

35:28.927 --> 35:30.754
Thank you, Mr. President.

35:36.795 --> 35:39.098
I keep goin'
back to Mexico.

35:39.234 --> 35:40.300
We were at the White House

35:40.436 --> 35:41.870
because the buyer never showed.

35:42.673 --> 35:46.265
Why hire SERPENT if you have
no intention on collecting?

35:46.401 --> 35:48.346
Maybe they were expecting
Captain America to come.

35:48.370 --> 35:50.610
What if the buyer wanted
Captain America to come?

35:50.745 --> 35:52.359
And what if they wanted
us at the White House?

35:52.383 --> 35:53.895
But how
would the buyer predict

35:53.919 --> 35:55.446
that we'd get the invite,

35:55.582 --> 35:57.352
or that you would invite Isaiah?

35:57.487 --> 35:59.686
The buyer must
be watching us somehow.

36:00.055 --> 36:01.355
Another thing.

36:01.490 --> 36:05.351
Ruth Bat-Seraph, Ross'
security advisor,

36:06.088 --> 36:07.587
find out what you can about her.

36:07.723 --> 36:08.754
Copy that.

36:08.890 --> 36:10.332
I'll call you back later.

36:41.298 --> 36:42.830
Target eliminated.

36:43.232 --> 36:45.162
Stand by for proof of death.

36:48.970 --> 36:50.207
Hmm.

37:10.658 --> 37:12.289
No way you came all
the way from Mexico

37:12.425 --> 37:13.690
just to blow up my car.

37:13.826 --> 37:16.266
So you must have made
up with the buyer.

37:17.727 --> 37:18.926
Get him on the phone.

37:19.062 --> 37:20.736
Let me see if I
can resolve this.

37:20.871 --> 37:23.130
"Resolve this"?

37:25.033 --> 37:26.732
The buyer told me everything.

37:27.368 --> 37:30.908
He mentioned that if you
survived the grenade,

37:31.043 --> 37:37.320
there was a 77% chance
you'd try to talk me down.

37:37.821 --> 37:38.688
Hmm.

37:38.824 --> 37:40.148
Look at that.

38:12.114 --> 38:14.388
The buyer told me
a lot actually.

38:14.523 --> 38:16.358
After he didn't show in Mexico,

38:16.494 --> 38:18.924
he agreed to pay me
double to take you out.

38:19.060 --> 38:23.992
What he doesn't know is that
I would kill you for free.

38:24.395 --> 38:29.339
How often do you get a chance
to kill Captain America?

38:40.945 --> 38:43.243
You're desperate
without your gear.

38:48.650 --> 38:49.959
Nope.

38:50.094 --> 38:51.519
Just a little meaner.

39:00.068 --> 39:01.068
Hello.

39:01.139 --> 39:02.538
Well done, Captain.

39:02.673 --> 39:05.006
But you're not going to
like what's coming next.

39:05.141 --> 39:06.475
Who is this?

39:14.443 --> 39:16.716
How
can we trust you to lead

39:16.851 --> 39:20.456
when you can't even keep
your own house in order?

39:21.723 --> 39:23.926
We have the shooters in custody.

39:24.395 --> 39:26.763
All I'm asking for is patience.

39:26.898 --> 39:28.261
Patience?

39:28.396 --> 39:30.290
From the Hulk Hunter?

39:31.400 --> 39:33.001
That was a long time ago.

39:33.137 --> 39:34.734
Well, Mr. President,

39:34.869 --> 39:38.441
I was almost killed in
your home yesterday.

39:38.576 --> 39:41.875
And today, you are still
locked in your bunker.

39:42.010 --> 39:45.571
You are not in a position
to be asking for anything.

39:45.707 --> 39:46.912
I agree.

39:47.047 --> 39:49.215
We should continue this
conversation another time.

39:49.351 --> 39:51.379
Gentlemen, wait.

39:51.515 --> 39:52.519
Please.

39:53.055 --> 39:56.258
This treaty is too important
to let it fall apart now.

39:56.394 --> 39:59.053
We made a promise to our people.

39:59.189 --> 40:01.563
We made a promise to the world.

40:02.626 --> 40:04.258
We must prevail.

40:05.533 --> 40:07.670
We'll need Japan to proceed.

40:07.805 --> 40:10.906
And Prime
Minister Ozaki's absence

40:11.041 --> 40:12.231
speaks volumes.

40:12.367 --> 40:14.409
I'll get Japan
back to the table.

40:14.545 --> 40:16.911
Ozaki and I go back a long way.

40:17.414 --> 40:19.306
He's running for re-election.

40:19.441 --> 40:22.678
He needs to assert
leadership on this treaty.

40:23.281 --> 40:27.016
All right, Mr. President,
we'll remain patient

40:27.151 --> 40:30.024
while you try to
get Japan on board.

40:30.259 --> 40:31.660
But if you don't,

40:31.795 --> 40:35.465
we'll have to take measures
into our own hands.

40:40.436 --> 40:41.904
I've gotta get out of here.

40:42.039 --> 40:43.039
Sit down.

40:43.132 --> 40:44.606
Sir, the sweep's not complete.

40:45.209 --> 40:47.367
The longer I stay here,

40:47.936 --> 40:49.409
the weaker I look.

40:59.818 --> 41:01.183
The hell happened to you?

41:02.524 --> 41:04.353
Sidewinder tracked me down.

41:04.489 --> 41:07.090
Well, it looks like
he did a lot more than that.

41:08.090 --> 41:09.664
He's in police custody now.

41:12.227 --> 41:14.102
- Shit, you good?
- I will be.

41:14.238 --> 41:16.330
Last call, trace it.

41:17.536 --> 41:18.574
All right.

41:24.775 --> 41:25.838
Yo, get this.

41:26.307 --> 41:28.076
Ross' advisor, Ruth Bat-Seraph,

41:28.479 --> 41:31.151
she was born in Israel and
trained in the Red Room.

41:31.286 --> 41:32.721
She's ex-Widow.

41:32.857 --> 41:34.628
That basically means stay
the hell out of her way.

41:34.652 --> 41:35.516
Trust me.

41:35.652 --> 41:36.757
Yep.

41:43.466 --> 41:44.631
Now, this is weird.

41:44.766 --> 41:48.297
Isaiah had Ross
in his crosshairs.

41:48.733 --> 41:49.864
Couldn't miss.

41:50.000 --> 41:51.498
I don't get it.

41:51.634 --> 41:53.754
Why go through all that
trouble just to not kill Ross?

41:53.936 --> 41:55.138
I don't know.

41:55.772 --> 41:56.975
Oh, shit.

41:57.111 --> 41:59.039
I think I located
Sidewinder's last caller.

41:59.542 --> 42:01.302
It's in the middle of
nowhere, West Virginia.

42:01.344 --> 42:03.719
It's just, like,
near some forest.

42:03.854 --> 42:05.955
Database only shows one name.

42:06.091 --> 42:07.986
Camp Echo One.

42:09.084 --> 42:10.758
No satellite imagery.

42:11.394 --> 42:13.222
Away from air traffic.

42:14.058 --> 42:16.330
No infrastructure in the area.

42:16.733 --> 42:18.294
- Do you think it's military?
- Yep.

42:18.429 --> 42:20.735
It's a place they send
you and you never leave.

42:28.446 --> 42:30.279
Ross told me stay out of this.

42:30.915 --> 42:33.473
Eh, he's just the President
of the United States.

42:47.894 --> 42:49.625
You don't have to come with me.

42:50.394 --> 42:52.793
Duh, I know. That's
what makes it so noble.

42:54.529 --> 42:56.065
Pack as much gear
as you can carry.

42:56.201 --> 42:57.905
I don't know when we'll be back.

42:58.941 --> 43:01.504
What, you mean like,
"right now" right now?

43:01.639 --> 43:03.008
Yeah.

43:03.741 --> 43:04.809
Oh, shit. Okay.

43:05.311 --> 43:07.109
Well, it's a long-ass
drive to West Virginia,

43:07.245 --> 43:08.613
so we're gonna need some snacks.

43:08.748 --> 43:10.152
Why did I invite you?

43:10.288 --> 43:12.050
What? Wait, wait, wait.

43:14.817 --> 43:15.857
Wait up!

43:16.259 --> 43:17.417
Ruth Bat-Seraph.

43:17.552 --> 43:19.595
Isaiah Bradley's
in holding cell 14.

43:19.730 --> 43:21.758
- The other shooters are in 15.
- Okay.

43:21.893 --> 43:23.032
Do you need an escort?

43:23.668 --> 43:25.308
Think I'll be just fine.

43:25.436 --> 43:27.098
- Thanks.
- Yes, ma'am.

43:34.679 --> 43:36.239
I'd like to speak to
them one at a time.

43:36.347 --> 43:38.139
Can you... Excuse me?

43:38.274 --> 43:40.749
Payumo. I'm talking
to you. Hey.

43:42.720 --> 43:44.310
Stop! Drop your weapon!

43:46.424 --> 43:48.416
Payumo, what are you doing?

43:48.818 --> 43:50.253
Drop it.

43:56.027 --> 43:59.328
♪ Call me Mr. Blue ♪

44:00.298 --> 44:05.901
♪ I'm Mr. Blue Wa-oo-wa-oo ♪

44:06.037 --> 44:07.501
♪ When you say... ♪

44:10.739 --> 44:12.258
Increase that cadence

44:12.282 --> 44:13.739
and resistance.

44:13.874 --> 44:14.953
Or do whatever the hell you
need to do to get there,

44:14.977 --> 44:16.245
all right?

44:16.614 --> 44:19.613
Just stay in your lane. Stay
in your lane. Here we go.

44:20.049 --> 44:21.217
Out to third!

44:21.353 --> 44:22.970
Eye on the prize. Eye
on the target, baby.

44:22.994 --> 44:25.189
- That's enough.
- Don't think about speed now.

44:25.325 --> 44:27.226
Think about direction.
Think about intention.

44:27.695 --> 44:29.859
If Dr. Eccles asks,

44:30.395 --> 44:34.704
you tell her I did
the whole five miles.

44:37.408 --> 44:39.835
That look.

44:40.204 --> 44:42.712
We touch down in Tokyo at 0600.

44:44.144 --> 44:46.847
You still think
this is a bad idea?

44:46.982 --> 44:48.356
Sir, whoever
orchestrated the attack

44:48.380 --> 44:50.280
on the White House
is still in the wild.

44:50.415 --> 44:52.617
International travel
brings security risks

44:52.753 --> 44:53.946
we can't anticipate.

44:54.716 --> 44:57.854
We barely got Congress
together on this thing.

44:58.390 --> 45:01.159
If we lose our
international partners,

45:01.762 --> 45:03.524
this treaty's toast.

45:04.832 --> 45:06.659
I have to make this work.

45:08.032 --> 45:09.294
Three miles and change.

45:09.430 --> 45:11.367
I'll let Dr. Eccles know.

45:11.736 --> 45:12.736
Five.

45:12.839 --> 45:14.343
- Five.
- Five.

45:14.479 --> 45:15.878
Do we have eyes on Wilson?

45:16.013 --> 45:18.405
He left the base a few hours
ago with Joaquin Torres.

45:18.540 --> 45:19.780
They ditched their smartphones.

45:19.845 --> 45:21.047
They're off-grid.

45:21.182 --> 45:22.747
Well, I don't want
a variable out there

45:22.882 --> 45:24.247
that I can't control.

45:24.383 --> 45:26.817
Get a team, pick him
up, bring him in.

45:26.953 --> 45:28.283
- Yes, sir.
- Yeah.

45:28.652 --> 45:30.497
Breaking
news out of Washington,

45:30.521 --> 45:32.291
President Ross is
on his way to Japan

45:32.427 --> 45:34.547
just a day after surviving
an assassination attempt...

45:34.593 --> 45:36.896
Bet you used to play this
old-ass game all the time.

45:37.032 --> 45:38.071
Damn
it. This is hard.

45:38.095 --> 45:39.528
Right.

45:39.664 --> 45:41.244
The
high-stakes diplomatic...

45:41.268 --> 45:42.828
How far are we
from Camp Echo One?

45:42.932 --> 45:45.234
...over
control of Celestial Island.

45:45.370 --> 45:47.704
We are about,
like, an hour away.

45:53.511 --> 45:56.149
Sam, shit. They just
shot up Isaiah's prison.

45:56.551 --> 45:57.576
Is he okay?

45:57.712 --> 45:59.881
Yeah, Isaiah's good,
but the others,

46:00.017 --> 46:01.017
they're dead.

46:01.148 --> 46:02.484
Shit.

46:03.119 --> 46:04.651
Should we go back?

46:06.758 --> 46:07.823
No.

46:07.959 --> 46:09.493
We keep going.

46:09.629 --> 46:11.773
The buyer is pretty smart,
but we're not taking the bait.

46:11.797 --> 46:14.964
Only way to help Isaiah is to
figure out who's behind this.

46:15.100 --> 46:16.668
And whoever is behind it,

46:17.170 --> 46:19.369
they do not want
us getting closer.

46:24.941 --> 46:25.941
Cooper.

46:26.241 --> 46:27.708
What's happening?

46:27.843 --> 46:30.046
Mr. President, as
a precautionary measure,

46:30.182 --> 46:31.715
I have moved the prisoner to...

46:33.551 --> 46:37.917
President Ross, I miss
our little visits.

46:38.286 --> 46:39.353
Tell me something.

46:39.488 --> 46:41.891
Do you ever stop to ask yourself

46:42.027 --> 46:43.595
who's playing the music?

46:43.730 --> 46:45.131
It's you.

46:45.600 --> 46:46.963
The White House,

46:47.099 --> 46:48.361
the assassination attempt.

46:48.496 --> 46:50.366
That's a way of putting it.

46:50.502 --> 46:53.467
I helped you
more than anyone else.

46:53.602 --> 46:55.168
Only to
get what you want.

46:55.304 --> 46:56.304
What do you want?

46:56.406 --> 46:58.175
I wanted my life back,

46:58.311 --> 46:59.974
but it's too late for that now.

47:00.110 --> 47:01.244
You've gotta...

47:01.380 --> 47:03.245
You gotta understand
my position.

47:03.380 --> 47:05.453
- I...
- Oh, I do.

47:05.822 --> 47:08.715
You let me rot in this prison.

47:08.850 --> 47:11.284
And it was my curse
to watch your betrayal

47:11.420 --> 47:13.456
written in probabilities.

47:14.292 --> 47:17.091
I'm making my own choices now.

47:17.227 --> 47:19.697
So many surprises left.

47:19.833 --> 47:20.968
When I'm done,

47:21.103 --> 47:23.597
everyone will know
just who you are,

47:23.732 --> 47:27.173
and Betty will
despise you even more.

47:27.842 --> 47:29.340
Goodbye, Mr. President.

47:32.882 --> 47:34.082
The hell is going on?

47:34.443 --> 47:36.284
I'm putting you in solitary.

47:36.419 --> 47:37.419
Yeah.

47:37.714 --> 47:40.050
Nobody's gonna put me
in solitary ever again.

47:40.186 --> 47:41.690
It's for your own protection.

47:42.326 --> 47:45.255
I'll tell you this one more
time for your protection,

47:45.391 --> 47:48.121
I ain't goin' in
a box ever again.

47:48.890 --> 47:51.294
I won't be able to
guarantee your safety.

47:51.430 --> 47:53.628
Safety ain't all it's
cracked up to be.

47:54.966 --> 47:56.233
You still think

47:56.369 --> 47:57.889
I had somethin' to
do with all of this?

47:58.234 --> 47:59.099
I don't know.

48:05.615 --> 48:06.807
Mr. President.

48:06.942 --> 48:08.257
I need you to drop
whatever you're doin'.

48:08.281 --> 48:09.943
Camp Echo One's
been compromised.

48:10.412 --> 48:11.987
Yes, Mr. President.

48:39.648 --> 48:40.675
This is it.

48:41.310 --> 48:42.344
Camp Echo One.

48:44.582 --> 48:46.987
Telescopes
must be a facade.

48:47.122 --> 48:48.991
We gotta see what's underneath.

48:52.491 --> 48:54.392
We've got
cameras and guards.

48:54.528 --> 48:57.197
Redwing, cut the fence
and go loop the feed.

49:02.031 --> 49:05.399
Yeah, we got a 28-second
window to get past the guards.

49:05.535 --> 49:07.537
We gotta do the door manually.

49:09.238 --> 49:11.673
Three, two, one,

49:12.075 --> 49:13.147
go.

49:26.827 --> 49:28.062
15 seconds.

49:28.198 --> 49:29.878
I'm trying, man!

49:30.160 --> 49:31.429
Shit!

50:18.710 --> 50:20.445
There's no
prisoners in here.

51:09.067 --> 51:11.562
Why is there a
lab in this prison?

51:19.437 --> 51:21.242
What the hell is this place?

52:33.818 --> 52:35.382
What the hell?

52:42.188 --> 52:43.188
Ozaki-san,

52:43.256 --> 52:44.690
I want to assure you

52:44.826 --> 52:47.929
America remains committed
to sharing our adamantium...

52:48.065 --> 52:49.856
...with the rest of the world.

52:49.992 --> 52:53.492
I trust Japan shares
that commitment.

52:53.894 --> 52:56.062
The world needs this treaty.

52:59.175 --> 53:01.309
Diplomacy must be hard for you.

53:01.944 --> 53:03.345
A man in a country

53:03.480 --> 53:06.248
so used to taking whatever
he wants by force.

53:06.750 --> 53:08.141
Excuse me?

53:08.276 --> 53:10.415
How else to explain your
theft of our adamantium,

53:10.550 --> 53:13.812
only to return it
to us in Washington.

53:14.215 --> 53:17.153
What you're accusing
us of is baseless

53:17.289 --> 53:19.284
and insulting.

53:19.420 --> 53:23.060
So, the information my
intelligence team received

53:23.195 --> 53:24.666
and verified

53:24.802 --> 53:26.598
is incorrect?

53:31.665 --> 53:33.066
Wh...

53:38.914 --> 53:40.106
I'm a fool.

53:41.847 --> 53:45.353
I'm a fool to negotiate
with someone so naive

53:45.488 --> 53:48.257
they don't realize
they're being played.

53:48.923 --> 53:50.149
Naive?

53:51.259 --> 53:53.095
If I'd stolen the sample,

53:53.497 --> 53:57.298
why would I order Captain
America to retrieve it?

53:57.434 --> 54:00.434
I suppose we'll
never know the truth.

54:06.105 --> 54:09.577
Whatever game you're playing,
Japan wants no part in it.

54:10.213 --> 54:12.138
Don't test us, Mr. President.

54:19.248 --> 54:21.613
He's got optogenetic
data on a lot of people.

54:22.183 --> 54:23.821
Don't make me look
up words, Joaquin.

54:23.956 --> 54:25.850
I think he's figured out
a way to plant commands

54:25.986 --> 54:27.026
into people's subconscious

54:27.063 --> 54:28.593
using flashes of light.

54:28.996 --> 54:31.799
This "Mr. Blue" song seems
to be some kind of trigger.

54:31.935 --> 54:33.225
Mind control.

54:33.803 --> 54:34.803
Yeah.

54:34.862 --> 54:36.602
That explains Isaiah.

54:42.475 --> 54:44.644
And that's more important.

54:45.046 --> 54:46.046
Take risks.

54:46.549 --> 54:48.909
Use those incredible
brains of yours.

54:49.045 --> 54:51.353
Wasn't half
bad-looking, was I?

54:57.654 --> 54:59.218
Samuel Sterns.

55:01.930 --> 55:04.766
You know, it takes
an awful lot to surprise me.

55:06.833 --> 55:10.171
There was an 89% chance
you'd turn around

55:10.307 --> 55:13.303
if I put Isaiah Bradley at risk,

55:13.439 --> 55:15.575
yet here you stand.

55:16.980 --> 55:17.980
You're the buyer.

55:18.112 --> 55:19.214
Indeed.

55:19.349 --> 55:21.516
Hiring SERPENT was
a necessary step

55:21.651 --> 55:24.651
to create a chain of
statistical certainties.

55:24.786 --> 55:27.081
Maybe you're not as smart
as you think you are.

55:27.748 --> 55:29.589
I am, actually.

55:29.724 --> 55:32.795
My mind sees it all,
every probable outcome.

55:33.464 --> 55:36.331
So you hire SERPENT to
steal the adamantium,

55:36.466 --> 55:38.664
shoot up Ross'
summit announcing it

55:38.799 --> 55:41.293
and now you're just
sitting here, waiting.

55:42.029 --> 55:43.561
Why do you wanna kill Ross?

55:43.697 --> 55:47.606
Why does everyone
think that I wanna kill Ross?

55:47.975 --> 55:52.107
Is it because he imprisoned
me here without a trial

55:52.242 --> 55:54.948
after an infusion of
gamma warped the structure

55:55.083 --> 55:56.308
of my brain?

56:00.153 --> 56:01.688
Damn.

56:01.823 --> 56:04.752
Once Ross discovered
how useful I could be,

56:04.888 --> 56:07.658
he kept me here for 16 years,

56:07.794 --> 56:10.664
turning my mind to
solving his problems.

56:10.966 --> 56:14.766
My solutions brought him the
highest office in the country.

56:16.264 --> 56:19.740
If I wanted Ross
dead, he'd be dead.

56:20.276 --> 56:21.606
Well, whatever you're doing,

56:21.975 --> 56:24.811
you're hurting a lot of
people, including my friend.

56:24.947 --> 56:27.841
So this is the last chance
I'm gonna give you to stop it.

56:27.976 --> 56:29.912
Why are you protecting him?

56:30.214 --> 56:32.720
Ross knows I'm responsible
for the White House,

56:32.855 --> 56:35.882
yet he's still letting
Isaiah sit in prison for it.

56:36.017 --> 56:37.549
You know he'll never change.

56:38.018 --> 56:39.094
Let me finish my work.

56:39.229 --> 56:40.526
I'm afraid I can't do that.

56:46.103 --> 56:49.262
Please don't be boring!

56:56.477 --> 56:58.046
You think they'll stop us?

56:58.182 --> 56:59.411
For long enough.

56:59.547 --> 57:01.473
You're a fascinating problem.

57:02.176 --> 57:04.418
But soon you'll
be off the board,

57:04.553 --> 57:06.754
so you don't surprise me again.

57:07.823 --> 57:09.983
This is messed up, man.
It's not even their choice.

57:10.118 --> 57:12.120
I know. Just try
and neutralize.

58:19.658 --> 58:20.658
Punk-ass.

58:36.145 --> 58:38.272
Stand down!

58:40.074 --> 58:41.675
I'm taking them in.

58:42.044 --> 58:43.651
I'll deal with these two.

58:45.650 --> 58:47.556
Okay.

59:12.242 --> 59:13.722
What the hell are
you guys doing here?

59:13.783 --> 59:16.212
Well, that's what I
should be asking you.

59:16.581 --> 59:17.581
Where's Sterns?

59:18.879 --> 59:21.254
If Sterns is in the wind,
we need to set a perimeter,

59:21.390 --> 59:22.849
roadblocks, air support.

59:22.985 --> 59:24.224
He can't have gone far.

59:24.360 --> 59:25.558
Why are you helping us?

59:26.060 --> 59:28.623
'Cause you were right. I
thought that was obvious.

59:29.226 --> 59:30.706
- Freeze!
- Oh. It's okay.

59:30.834 --> 59:32.636
We have orders to take
Captain America into custody.

59:32.660 --> 59:34.597
You already have one
Captain America in custody.

59:34.732 --> 59:35.932
You want another?

59:36.068 --> 59:37.342
You're under arrest
for trespassing

59:37.366 --> 59:39.333
on restricted
government property.

59:40.501 --> 59:41.835
Being right always go like this?

59:41.970 --> 59:43.370
Most of the time.

59:45.607 --> 59:47.911
I have the clearances.
It's been a long day.

59:48.046 --> 59:50.345
She's ex-Widow.
Just zap the guy.

59:50.480 --> 59:52.781
These orders come from
the President himself.

59:52.916 --> 59:54.112
Get them out of here.

59:54.248 --> 59:55.714
Then we'll just call him.

59:57.151 --> 59:58.416
Ruth, uncuff us now!

59:58.552 --> 01:00:00.393
♪ I'm Mr. Blue Wa-oo-wa-oo ♪

01:00:00.529 --> 01:00:01.959
♪ When you say... ♪

01:00:02.095 --> 01:00:03.368
Oh, shit, shit, shit,
shit. Not again.

01:00:03.392 --> 01:00:05.601
- Run!
- Go, go, go. Come on.

01:00:13.572 --> 01:00:14.241
Go!

01:00:19.274 --> 01:00:20.418
Mr. President,

01:00:20.442 --> 01:00:22.815
Japan's claim seems to be true.

01:00:23.184 --> 01:00:25.648
We're trying to determine
the point of the breach.

01:00:26.251 --> 01:00:28.347
Sir, we have to tell
Ozaki's team something.

01:00:28.483 --> 01:00:29.817
We've got to stop the bleeding.

01:00:29.953 --> 01:00:31.216
I need some time alone.

01:00:31.352 --> 01:00:32.961
We don't have much time, sir.

01:00:33.097 --> 01:00:35.859
Ozaki just decided to advance
his navy on Celestial Island.

01:00:36.394 --> 01:00:38.274
He intends to secure the
adamantium for himself.

01:00:38.368 --> 01:00:39.901
Jesus.

01:00:40.037 --> 01:00:41.905
France and India are drawing
up occupation strategies...

01:00:41.929 --> 01:00:43.648
Mr. President, I suggest that
we return to DC immediately.

01:00:43.672 --> 01:00:45.268
- No, I disagree.
- Immediately.

01:00:45.403 --> 01:00:46.976
We are going to lose our
opportunity with Ozaki.

01:00:47.000 --> 01:00:48.480
We need to regroup and figure
out a different solution.

01:00:48.504 --> 01:00:50.007
We can't do that.
No, absolutely not!

01:00:50.142 --> 01:00:51.214
We need to ask for
another meeting, sir.

01:00:51.238 --> 01:00:52.405
If we call on Ozaki now,

01:00:52.541 --> 01:00:54.142
and try to reach out
to him, we can...

01:00:54.278 --> 01:00:55.846
We're not gonna
miss the argument.

01:00:55.981 --> 01:00:57.452
We have to have another meeting!

01:01:10.925 --> 01:01:16.031
I want Carrier Strike Group
Five deployed immediately.

01:01:16.166 --> 01:01:17.597
Tell 'em I'm on
my way there now.

01:01:17.733 --> 01:01:20.275
Sir, are we seriously
talking about taking control

01:01:20.410 --> 01:01:21.543
of Japan's adamantium?

01:01:21.679 --> 01:01:24.208
I'm not going home empty-handed.

01:01:24.344 --> 01:01:27.809
If only one country is
going to control adamantium,

01:01:27.945 --> 01:01:29.718
it's going to be us.

01:01:34.621 --> 01:01:36.516
Make the call!

01:01:39.129 --> 01:01:40.422
Taylor!

01:01:40.557 --> 01:01:42.039
The
President has informed me

01:01:42.063 --> 01:01:43.303
that we need to move
Strike Group Five

01:01:43.327 --> 01:01:44.890
to Celestial Island immediately.

01:01:45.025 --> 01:01:48.363
I want to be en route to the
Indian Ocean within the hour.

01:01:48.498 --> 01:01:52.367
Mr. President, this is
extremely dangerous.

01:01:53.135 --> 01:01:54.135
If a war breaks out...

01:01:54.268 --> 01:01:56.140
I was a wartime general.

01:01:56.876 --> 01:01:59.275
Now I'm a wartime president.

01:02:02.012 --> 01:02:03.719
Yes, sir, Mr. President.

01:02:27.939 --> 01:02:29.272
What are we doing here?

01:02:29.407 --> 01:02:31.345
You say Ross' orders was
to take us into custody

01:02:31.481 --> 01:02:33.474
so I called in a favor.

01:02:34.110 --> 01:02:35.510
Thanks for doing this.

01:02:35.645 --> 01:02:37.949
No problem, Cap. Brass
never makes it down here.

01:02:38.084 --> 01:02:39.783
Terminal's set up, ready to go.

01:02:40.485 --> 01:02:42.491
You sure you can knock
out Sterns' mind control?

01:02:42.626 --> 01:02:43.986
I should be able
to run a program

01:02:44.122 --> 01:02:45.553
that blocks the light signals

01:02:45.689 --> 01:02:47.926
that Sterns has been sending
out to control people.

01:02:48.062 --> 01:02:50.359
What if he's already
gotten someone?

01:02:51.094 --> 01:02:52.460
That's a good point.

01:02:56.769 --> 01:02:57.936
Are you crazy?

01:02:58.072 --> 01:03:00.469
♪ I'm Mr. Blue Wa-oo-wa-oo ♪

01:03:00.604 --> 01:03:04.941
♪ When you say you
love me Oh, Mr. Blue ♪

01:03:05.076 --> 01:03:06.174
We're clear here, at least.

01:03:06.309 --> 01:03:07.807
You have anybody that you trust

01:03:07.943 --> 01:03:10.056
that can take a look at these
and tell me what's in 'em?

01:03:10.080 --> 01:03:11.549
Sure, I got someone.

01:03:11.684 --> 01:03:12.720
I'll get on it.

01:03:12.856 --> 01:03:15.087
- Thanks. Our guy here?
- Through there.

01:03:15.853 --> 01:03:17.089
Listen in.

01:03:20.722 --> 01:03:23.227
I'm amazed
you're still standing.

01:03:23.362 --> 01:03:26.532
Most men don't survive
an axe to the gut.

01:03:26.668 --> 01:03:27.995
Kevlar weave, I presume?

01:03:28.130 --> 01:03:29.295
Perks of the job.

01:03:30.064 --> 01:03:33.032
You said you were gonna find
the man who wasted your time.

01:03:33.435 --> 01:03:34.737
I wanna know what you learned.

01:03:34.873 --> 01:03:35.973
Samuel Sterns.

01:03:36.108 --> 01:03:38.004
Gruesome fella, don't you think?

01:03:38.139 --> 01:03:39.711
I've seen worse.

01:03:39.847 --> 01:03:40.939
Not without your Avengers.

01:03:43.114 --> 01:03:44.650
Full immunity and I'll talk.

01:03:44.785 --> 01:03:45.880
You're crazy.

01:03:46.015 --> 01:03:47.384
Who you kiddin'?

01:03:47.519 --> 01:03:49.034
You're here because
you're all out of options.

01:03:49.058 --> 01:03:50.618
You heard what he did
to those shooters.

01:03:50.819 --> 01:03:53.457
A guy like Sterns doesn't
like loose ends alive.

01:03:54.789 --> 01:03:58.625
Reduced sentence,
Allenwood, my own cell.

01:03:59.395 --> 01:04:01.133
Lemme hear what you got first.

01:04:03.502 --> 01:04:06.298
You know, it was my old
unit that found Sterns

01:04:06.434 --> 01:04:07.674
in the wreckage of Harlem.

01:04:08.377 --> 01:04:10.602
They said he'd been infected
with Bruce Banner's blood,

01:04:10.738 --> 01:04:12.612
but it didn't give him strength.

01:04:12.747 --> 01:04:14.013
What did it give him?

01:04:14.149 --> 01:04:17.017
A mind capable of
impossible calculations.

01:04:17.651 --> 01:04:19.245
Ross being Ross,

01:04:19.380 --> 01:04:20.887
he saw an opportunity.

01:04:21.290 --> 01:04:24.150
Instead of removing the
gamma from Sterns' blood,

01:04:24.285 --> 01:04:26.691
he upped the dose.

01:04:27.294 --> 01:04:30.292
Made Sterns his own
personal think tank,

01:04:30.694 --> 01:04:34.028
creating technology and
weapons for the state.

01:04:34.430 --> 01:04:36.503
Holy shit.

01:04:36.939 --> 01:04:38.331
Why did Sterns go along with it?

01:04:38.466 --> 01:04:41.072
Camp Echo One was the stick.

01:04:41.207 --> 01:04:44.242
I imagine a pardon
was the carrot.

01:04:45.909 --> 01:04:50.045
Ross told Sterns he'd let him
go once he became president.

01:04:50.180 --> 01:04:52.745
And yet, here we are.

01:04:54.652 --> 01:04:58.255
So Sterns hired you to
steal Japan's adamantium

01:04:58.391 --> 01:05:00.687
knowing it would divide
the two countries.

01:05:03.263 --> 01:05:05.460
He paid us through
a CIA black fund.

01:05:05.596 --> 01:05:08.328
That could kill the
treaty and start a war.

01:05:08.697 --> 01:05:11.199
And Ross would be
blamed for the chaos.

01:05:11.702 --> 01:05:14.007
How do you think a man
with Ross' temperament

01:05:14.143 --> 01:05:17.440
will deal with being
caught in a trap?

01:05:18.577 --> 01:05:21.945
If you break out of
Allenwood, I'll find you.

01:05:22.081 --> 01:05:25.012
When I break out, Captain,

01:05:25.381 --> 01:05:27.483
you won't walk away alive.

01:05:29.122 --> 01:05:30.451
- Did you know?
- Of course not.

01:05:30.586 --> 01:05:32.587
But Ross is not
that man anymore.

01:05:32.722 --> 01:05:35.062
None of us have to be
defined by our past.

01:05:35.197 --> 01:05:37.862
Cap, my guy needs 24
hours on the pills.

01:05:37.998 --> 01:05:39.163
Okay. We need to get to DC

01:05:39.299 --> 01:05:41.064
and tell Ross what
Sterns is planning.

01:05:41.199 --> 01:05:42.698
President Ross isn't in DC.

01:05:43.101 --> 01:05:44.432
He's on the USS Milius.

01:05:44.568 --> 01:05:46.304
They just moved into
the Indian Ocean.

01:05:46.439 --> 01:05:48.336
Japan's warships are
also in proximity.

01:05:48.471 --> 01:05:51.144
Shit. Suit up.
We need to move.

01:05:57.784 --> 01:05:58.784
May I help you?

01:05:58.851 --> 01:05:59.917
Hello, Admiral.

01:06:00.052 --> 01:06:01.584
May I use your phone?

01:06:01.719 --> 01:06:03.724
Hey,
honey. Who's at the door?

01:06:08.764 --> 01:06:09.993
Holy shit.

01:06:10.396 --> 01:06:11.994
You ever see anything like this?

01:06:12.130 --> 01:06:13.262
No, I haven't.

01:06:39.791 --> 01:06:41.734
Let me do the talking
or he'll never listen.

01:06:41.758 --> 01:06:44.027
I haven't seen Ross like
this since the army.

01:06:44.163 --> 01:06:45.695
He better snap out of it.

01:06:45.831 --> 01:06:48.498
Because whatever Sterns is
planning, it's happening soon.

01:06:49.833 --> 01:06:52.337
I want a fleet of
F-18s ready to catapult.

01:06:52.472 --> 01:06:55.010
If they turn that
ship around, I want...

01:06:56.339 --> 01:06:57.505
What's he doing here?

01:06:57.641 --> 01:06:59.712
I told you not to
get involved, Wilson.

01:06:59.848 --> 01:07:00.913
I brought him, sir.

01:07:01.049 --> 01:07:02.314
I want him outta here!

01:07:02.450 --> 01:07:04.054
Sir, you asked me to
run this investigation,

01:07:04.078 --> 01:07:07.152
- and the situation is...
- Don't bother with excuses.

01:07:07.288 --> 01:07:09.721
You had a simple
job and you failed.

01:07:09.857 --> 01:07:10.885
Mr. President,

01:07:11.722 --> 01:07:14.193
we've uncovered intel
at Camp Echo One

01:07:14.329 --> 01:07:16.690
that could put millions
of lives at risk.

01:07:16.826 --> 01:07:19.300
Now, you and I both
know Isaiah's innocent.

01:07:20.303 --> 01:07:22.833
I'm happy to have this
conversation in public,

01:07:22.968 --> 01:07:24.204
if you like.

01:07:31.380 --> 01:07:33.609
This is crazy.
Japan's supposed to be our...

01:07:33.745 --> 01:07:36.012
Jackal?

01:07:36.148 --> 01:07:37.615
Jackal, do you copy?

01:07:38.886 --> 01:07:41.320
♪ I'm Mr. Blue ♪

01:07:43.089 --> 01:07:44.653
Make it quick, Wilson.

01:07:46.228 --> 01:07:48.119
I've got Japan's fleet on my ass

01:07:48.254 --> 01:07:50.127
trying to make it to
that island before we do.

01:07:50.263 --> 01:07:51.694
That's exactly what he wants.

01:07:51.829 --> 01:07:54.496
Sterns has been pulling
the strings on everything.

01:07:54.631 --> 01:07:56.430
SERPENT's theft
of the adamantium,

01:07:56.566 --> 01:07:58.101
the attack on the White House.

01:07:58.236 --> 01:08:00.036
The CIA leak to Japan.

01:08:00.772 --> 01:08:02.977
He's pitting you and
Japan against each other

01:08:03.113 --> 01:08:04.772
to ensure that this
moment happens.

01:08:04.908 --> 01:08:07.113
How the hell did he do
all that from prison?

01:08:07.249 --> 01:08:10.215
Mind control. He
created a technology

01:08:10.351 --> 01:08:11.917
that allowed him to
control the minds

01:08:12.052 --> 01:08:13.654
of anyone he targeted.

01:08:13.923 --> 01:08:15.316
Including maybe you, sir.

01:08:21.221 --> 01:08:23.626
Have you been feelin'
like yourself lately?

01:08:29.937 --> 01:08:31.269
Of course I have.

01:08:31.404 --> 01:08:33.497
But he has your
data, sir. Why?

01:08:33.633 --> 01:08:34.700
I don't know.

01:08:35.269 --> 01:08:38.644
If he can control minds,
surely he can hack files.

01:08:38.780 --> 01:08:41.710
The logs show that you visited
Camp Echo One numerous times.

01:08:41.845 --> 01:08:46.348
To ensure a high-value
prisoner was secure.

01:08:46.484 --> 01:08:47.682
Yeah, but the scans, the EKG,

01:08:47.817 --> 01:08:49.789
the blood work was
all taken there, sir.

01:08:49.925 --> 01:08:51.091
This is ridiculous.

01:08:51.227 --> 01:08:52.684
Mr. President,
answer the question.

01:08:52.819 --> 01:08:54.827
I don't have to answer you!

01:08:54.963 --> 01:08:56.263
Why visit a Black Site,

01:08:56.398 --> 01:08:57.975
- in the middle of nowhere...
- Wilson, stop!

01:08:57.999 --> 01:08:59.432
I order you to stop!

01:08:59.568 --> 01:09:00.937
- ...to conduct these tests?
- I order you to stop!

01:09:00.961 --> 01:09:03.065
- Why?
- Because I was dying,

01:09:03.200 --> 01:09:04.267
goddamn it!

01:09:08.869 --> 01:09:11.773
Because my heart was failing!

01:09:13.448 --> 01:09:16.041
No one could figure
it out until he did.

01:09:20.454 --> 01:09:24.082
These things have kept me alive.

01:09:25.028 --> 01:09:27.786
And in return, I gave him hope

01:09:27.922 --> 01:09:30.055
that he might get his life back.

01:09:31.000 --> 01:09:34.426
He got a lab to do the work.

01:09:35.062 --> 01:09:37.029
I even tried to get
him moved but...

01:09:37.164 --> 01:09:39.174
But you couldn't risk
losing the pills.

01:09:44.678 --> 01:09:47.414
After your friend the
Hulk and the Abomination

01:09:47.549 --> 01:09:51.650
destroyed Harlem, someone
had to take the fall.

01:09:52.052 --> 01:09:53.485
Sterns was just...

01:09:54.219 --> 01:09:56.257
collateral damage.

01:09:59.491 --> 01:10:02.296
I have dedicated my entire life

01:10:03.031 --> 01:10:05.090
to serving this country.

01:10:08.863 --> 01:10:11.096
The one person that matters...

01:10:12.272 --> 01:10:14.666
doesn't seem to understand.

01:10:15.502 --> 01:10:22.283
Betty never forgave me for
sending the army after Banner.

01:10:24.811 --> 01:10:27.013
I had to survive...

01:10:31.686 --> 01:10:34.018
so that my daughter knew

01:10:34.153 --> 01:10:36.697
that there was
more to her father.

01:10:37.533 --> 01:10:39.428
That I'm the same man
that used to take her

01:10:39.563 --> 01:10:41.533
to see the cherry blossoms.

01:10:43.203 --> 01:10:45.339
She still can, sir.

01:10:47.702 --> 01:10:49.376
I know what it's like...

01:10:51.446 --> 01:10:53.974
to feel you have
somethin' to prove.

01:10:55.174 --> 01:10:57.450
Everyone only seeing one thing.

01:10:59.080 --> 01:11:01.447
But when showing
there's more to you,

01:11:02.083 --> 01:11:04.481
it's not about when
times are easy.

01:11:05.051 --> 01:11:07.757
It's about moments like this.

01:11:09.630 --> 01:11:12.562
Now, we're here because
Sterns wants revenge

01:11:12.698 --> 01:11:15.103
and doesn't care if
he incites a war.

01:11:15.238 --> 01:11:17.695
We're playing right
into his hand.

01:11:18.097 --> 01:11:20.031
Mr. President,
two of our F-18s

01:11:20.167 --> 01:11:22.307
just fired on the
Japanese fleet.

01:11:25.305 --> 01:11:27.539
Keep
hailing those pilots.

01:11:28.342 --> 01:11:30.808
Damage
to Japanese fleet minimal.

01:11:31.278 --> 01:11:32.827
Ready
air defense systems.

01:11:32.851 --> 01:11:34.987
What the hell
are those pilots doing?

01:11:35.122 --> 01:11:36.156
Call them back in.

01:11:36.291 --> 01:11:37.491
We tried, sir.

01:11:37.558 --> 01:11:38.918
Jackal and Whiskey
won't respond.

01:11:39.054 --> 01:11:40.590
We gotta get our
birds in the air.

01:11:40.725 --> 01:11:42.854
You have two ready
to fly now, sir.

01:11:44.767 --> 01:11:45.767
Go.

01:12:00.514 --> 01:12:01.906
Sterns
got to our pilots

01:12:02.042 --> 01:12:03.478
before I shut down the system.

01:12:04.147 --> 01:12:05.787
We
need to get the Japanese

01:12:05.811 --> 01:12:06.845
out of the air.

01:12:07.281 --> 01:12:08.881
Stay close and don't
get yourself killed.

01:12:09.016 --> 01:12:10.721
No dying, copy that.

01:12:16.791 --> 01:12:18.524
Return to your fleet.

01:12:35.978 --> 01:12:37.258
Jackal's headed

01:12:37.285 --> 01:12:38.683
towards the Japanese fleet.

01:12:39.947 --> 01:12:41.779
Shit! He just fired on them.

01:12:42.382 --> 01:12:44.591
Mr. President, do not
send more fighters up.

01:12:44.726 --> 01:12:47.494
We need Japan to see we're
trying to deescalate.

01:13:01.843 --> 01:13:04.544
Sir, six
Japanese missiles inbound.

01:13:07.183 --> 01:13:08.680
Launch intercept missiles.

01:13:21.431 --> 01:13:23.024
Damn,
two got through.

01:13:23.160 --> 01:13:25.257
Take
the one on the right.

01:13:31.437 --> 01:13:33.441
Redwing, a little help.

01:13:52.323 --> 01:13:55.155
Sir, you need to convince
Japan to ground their planes.

01:13:58.799 --> 01:14:00.693
This is what we expected

01:14:00.829 --> 01:14:02.328
from a Ross presidency.

01:14:02.464 --> 01:14:05.330
Mr. Prime Minister, two of
our pilots have gone rogue.

01:14:05.465 --> 01:14:07.605
Call off your planes.
We're being manipulated.

01:14:07.741 --> 01:14:09.021
Certainly.

01:14:09.241 --> 01:14:10.610
By you.

01:14:10.745 --> 01:14:12.713
Hiding your assassins
behind Captain America.

01:14:13.649 --> 01:14:17.111
He's trying to bring
them down now, sir.

01:14:17.246 --> 01:14:20.178
If those pilots are not
taking orders from you,

01:14:20.314 --> 01:14:24.019
then who gives them
their commands?

01:14:25.392 --> 01:14:26.587
That's what I thought.

01:14:31.224 --> 01:14:32.632
Mr. President?

01:14:36.763 --> 01:14:39.967
Ah,
now we're getting somewhere.

01:14:40.102 --> 01:14:43.705
That fire in the
belly. The rage.

01:14:43.841 --> 01:14:45.771
Why don't you just let it out?

01:14:45.907 --> 01:14:47.047
Are you all right, sir?

01:14:48.782 --> 01:14:51.519
I
just need a moment.

01:14:56.726 --> 01:14:59.026
Joaquin,
Whiskey's coming at you.

01:14:59.162 --> 01:15:00.759
Copy that.

01:15:07.562 --> 01:15:10.931
Sam, once we're done, you
gotta teach me your moves!

01:15:17.678 --> 01:15:20.174
Altitude. Altitude.

01:15:23.712 --> 01:15:24.712
Altitude.

01:15:26.788 --> 01:15:28.413
Whiskey's
away. Send rescue.

01:15:28.548 --> 01:15:30.251
Roger, sending rescue.

01:15:30.387 --> 01:15:31.935
You have two Japanese fighters
coming up on your tail.

01:15:31.959 --> 01:15:33.985
Why the hell
are they still chasing us?

01:15:34.121 --> 01:15:35.421
We're trying to help them.

01:15:35.556 --> 01:15:37.001
Because
Ross won't tell them

01:15:37.025 --> 01:15:38.456
who's really behind this.

01:15:41.296 --> 01:15:43.897
All that
hatred you try to hide,

01:15:44.300 --> 01:15:48.404
all the ugliness, it's
still there, Ross,

01:15:48.806 --> 01:15:51.344
smoldering behind the eyes.

01:16:08.061 --> 01:16:10.356
Joaquin,
I'm goin' after Jackal.

01:16:11.691 --> 01:16:14.327
Roger that.
I'll keep these guys busy.

01:16:19.269 --> 01:16:21.203
What have you done
to me, you bastard?

01:16:21.338 --> 01:16:24.912
What we agreed
on. Maybe a hair more.

01:16:25.281 --> 01:16:26.404
You poisoned me!

01:16:26.539 --> 01:16:28.414
Stop taking
the pills then.

01:16:28.549 --> 01:16:30.650
But we both know you won't.

01:16:30.786 --> 01:16:34.888
Give me what I want.
Stop fighting it.

01:16:35.024 --> 01:16:36.181
No!

01:17:06.747 --> 01:17:09.448
Sam, Jackal just
fired his last missiles!

01:17:14.388 --> 01:17:16.192
I got one. Going
after the another.

01:17:16.327 --> 01:17:18.447
- Back off! I'll get it!
- No, no! I got it.

01:17:18.533 --> 01:17:20.195
- Back off!
- I got it.

01:17:23.402 --> 01:17:24.705
Joaquin!

01:17:32.407 --> 01:17:34.007
Joaquin's down! I'm
goin' after him.

01:17:34.143 --> 01:17:35.303
We'll send search and rescue.

01:17:35.384 --> 01:17:37.247
You have to stop Jackal.

01:17:37.383 --> 01:17:38.383
Damn it!

01:17:38.412 --> 01:17:40.453
I'm putting an end to this now.

01:17:40.589 --> 01:17:42.716
Give in to your rage.

01:17:43.352 --> 01:17:46.384
I'm taking your
legacy as we speak.

01:17:46.520 --> 01:17:49.124
Come on, Ross.
You're almost there.

01:17:49.526 --> 01:17:54.158
You can rip their fleet
apart with your bare hands,

01:17:54.294 --> 01:17:56.198
and kill Captain America.

01:18:01.639 --> 01:18:02.639
Oh, shit.

01:18:09.081 --> 01:18:11.719
Let the
monster inside you out.

01:18:19.620 --> 01:18:22.162
Altitude,
altitude, altitude.

01:18:22.565 --> 01:18:25.528
Altitude, altitude, altitude.

01:18:25.930 --> 01:18:27.894
Unleash your anger.

01:18:28.030 --> 01:18:29.527
Unleash your hatred.

01:18:29.663 --> 01:18:31.464
Redwing, stabilize!

01:18:36.537 --> 01:18:38.939
Nothing
can stop you, Ross.

01:18:39.075 --> 01:18:41.045
You could crush them all.

01:18:55.893 --> 01:18:57.259
Mr. President?

01:18:58.631 --> 01:19:00.725
Sir. Are you okay?

01:19:00.860 --> 01:19:03.362
Captain America neutralized
the rogue pilots.

01:19:03.498 --> 01:19:05.634
Japan's recalling their planes.

01:19:07.400 --> 01:19:09.133
Get Ozaki back on the line.

01:19:09.269 --> 01:19:11.141
We can fix this.

01:19:28.858 --> 01:19:29.924
Where's Joaquin?

01:19:30.060 --> 01:19:31.696
Med-evac just got to him.

01:19:31.831 --> 01:19:33.328
Thank God.

01:19:41.471 --> 01:19:43.204
A crisis
was narrowly avoided

01:19:43.340 --> 01:19:44.975
when a brief dogfight broke out

01:19:45.111 --> 01:19:47.139
between Japanese and
US military forces

01:19:47.274 --> 01:19:49.045
over Celestial Island.

01:19:49.181 --> 01:19:51.080
US Air Force Captain
Joaquin Torres

01:19:51.216 --> 01:19:53.078
was shot down
during the skirmish,

01:19:53.214 --> 01:19:54.580
and is now in surgery at

01:19:54.715 --> 01:19:57.050
Walter Reed National
Military Medical Center.

01:19:57.186 --> 01:19:59.122
His condition is critical.

01:19:59.258 --> 01:20:00.498
Here,
give me that clamp.

01:20:00.522 --> 01:20:02.060
Gonna
need to pack this!

01:20:03.323 --> 01:20:04.997
Suction!

01:20:06.132 --> 01:20:08.231
I can't see anything.
More suction.

01:20:08.832 --> 01:20:10.134
Retractors.

01:20:14.807 --> 01:20:16.470
It's a private room.

01:20:18.544 --> 01:20:19.770
Go away.

01:20:25.850 --> 01:20:27.118
I missed you, too.

01:20:33.556 --> 01:20:38.492
I hate to admit it,
I'm glad you're here.

01:20:45.503 --> 01:20:47.765
You looked good out there
on that six o'clock.

01:20:48.434 --> 01:20:50.241
But then I saw this.

01:20:51.177 --> 01:20:53.573
The doctors had to
restart his heart.

01:20:55.342 --> 01:20:56.983
They don't know if...

01:20:59.885 --> 01:21:01.317
This isn't your fault.

01:21:02.383 --> 01:21:04.386
It makes me think of Steve.

01:21:05.555 --> 01:21:08.623
How many alien invasions
did he stop again?

01:21:08.759 --> 01:21:09.855
Two.

01:21:09.991 --> 01:21:10.991
Two.

01:21:12.862 --> 01:21:14.132
Wow.

01:21:16.170 --> 01:21:18.697
What made me think
I could follow that?

01:21:21.507 --> 01:21:26.144
I should've took the serum.
Like Steve, like you.

01:21:27.646 --> 01:21:28.646
Why?

01:21:31.518 --> 01:21:35.318
Because this is all startin'
to seem much bigger than me.

01:21:36.686 --> 01:21:41.825
Ross, he asked me to
restart the Avengers, Buck.

01:21:41.960 --> 01:21:43.489
But Joaquin's in here,

01:21:43.625 --> 01:21:46.859
Isaiah's in prison,
and Sterns...

01:21:47.762 --> 01:21:52.203
I had him. I had Sterns
right in my hands.

01:21:53.068 --> 01:21:54.301
And he got away.

01:21:54.703 --> 01:21:57.136
He damn near pushed us
to the brink of war,

01:21:57.272 --> 01:21:59.012
because I wasn't...

01:22:01.013 --> 01:22:02.741
Say what you need to say.

01:22:08.250 --> 01:22:10.452
Steve made a mistake.

01:22:11.659 --> 01:22:12.855
No, he didn't.

01:22:12.991 --> 01:22:14.890
He gave you that shield

01:22:15.459 --> 01:22:17.695
not because you're
the strongest,

01:22:17.831 --> 01:22:19.296
but because you're you.

01:22:23.269 --> 01:22:24.929
You think if you had that serum

01:22:25.065 --> 01:22:27.836
you'd be able to protect all
the people you care about.

01:22:28.239 --> 01:22:30.807
Steve had it, and he couldn't.

01:22:31.577 --> 01:22:34.377
You're a human being, and
you're doing your best.

01:22:35.414 --> 01:22:37.384
Steve gave people
something to believe in.

01:22:37.519 --> 01:22:38.549
But you...

01:22:39.252 --> 01:22:41.989
you give 'em something
to aspire to.

01:22:45.523 --> 01:22:47.323
Did your speechwriters
help you with that?

01:22:47.459 --> 01:22:49.059
They did, yeah. The
ending, a little bit.

01:22:49.159 --> 01:22:50.325
Well, did you like it?

01:22:50.461 --> 01:22:52.195
No, no, it was
good. Solid B-plus.

01:22:52.331 --> 01:22:54.665
- Emotional.
- Yeah, very. I felt it.

01:22:54.800 --> 01:22:55.830
But just enough.

01:22:55.965 --> 01:22:57.103
Yeah.

01:22:58.302 --> 01:23:00.337
Listen, I gotta catch a plane.

01:23:00.472 --> 01:23:03.406
I have a campaign
fundraiser. It's so stupid.

01:23:07.916 --> 01:23:09.984
It's gonna be all right, man.

01:23:15.888 --> 01:23:17.222
Thanks, Buck.

01:23:18.187 --> 01:23:20.126
I love you, buddy.

01:23:29.266 --> 01:23:31.001
- Was that...
- Yep.

01:23:31.437 --> 01:23:35.207
Future Congressman
James Buchanan Barnes.

01:23:38.873 --> 01:23:41.673
He's taller in real
life, nice smile too,

01:23:41.809 --> 01:23:44.584
good amount of
teeth, great posture.

01:23:44.720 --> 01:23:46.616
He's 110 years old.

01:23:47.085 --> 01:23:48.285
I can work with that.

01:23:48.420 --> 01:23:49.827
While
the investigation

01:23:49.851 --> 01:23:51.429
into the White House
assassination attempt

01:23:51.453 --> 01:23:52.852
and the shocking shooting at

01:23:52.987 --> 01:23:55.828
Joint Base Anacostia-Bolling
is still under way,

01:23:55.963 --> 01:23:58.063
Isaiah Bradley is set to go

01:23:58.198 --> 01:23:59.478
before a military
judge tomorrow.

01:23:59.568 --> 01:24:00.761
I need some air.

01:24:00.896 --> 01:24:02.816
It's a
fall from grace for a man

01:24:02.865 --> 01:24:05.631
brought out from the
shadows by Captain America.

01:24:05.767 --> 01:24:08.102
Just two years after
being exonerated

01:24:08.238 --> 01:24:09.672
for unjust charges,

01:24:09.808 --> 01:24:12.605
Bradley now finds himself
held in solitary confinement

01:24:12.741 --> 01:24:16.314
and facing a possible
death sentence.

01:24:27.724 --> 01:24:30.361
Okay,
reset. Let's go again.

01:24:32.194 --> 01:24:33.463
Talk to me.

01:24:33.598 --> 01:24:35.080
Dunphy, you
check out my report?

01:24:35.104 --> 01:24:36.209
All right, what am I looking at?

01:24:36.233 --> 01:24:37.696
Those pills you gave me,

01:24:37.832 --> 01:24:39.232
they're loaded with
gamma radiation,

01:24:39.306 --> 01:24:41.271
engineered to be
absorbed into the blood.

01:24:41.407 --> 01:24:42.940
Where the hell
did you get these?

01:24:43.076 --> 01:24:45.112
Shit. I gotta make a call.

01:24:52.387 --> 01:24:56.653
This sound is currently
affecting your equilibrium.

01:24:57.122 --> 01:24:58.822
When I turn this dial,

01:24:59.291 --> 01:25:01.627
it will disrupt your heartbeat.

01:25:02.263 --> 01:25:04.865
I take no pleasure
in your death,

01:25:05.234 --> 01:25:07.558
but I can't have you
calling the Captain.

01:25:07.693 --> 01:25:10.500
Who are you?

01:25:11.300 --> 01:25:13.338
Isn't it obvious?

01:25:13.973 --> 01:25:15.632
I'm the hero.

01:25:37.864 --> 01:25:39.265
Sir.

01:25:41.136 --> 01:25:42.602
Agent Taylor.

01:25:43.004 --> 01:25:44.103
Just wanted to let you know

01:25:44.238 --> 01:25:45.635
that every guest
has been screened,

01:25:45.770 --> 01:25:47.650
and we also did three
sweeps of the Rose Garden.

01:25:47.907 --> 01:25:48.936
Thank you.

01:25:49.639 --> 01:25:51.607
- See you out there.
- Yes, sir.

01:26:11.330 --> 01:26:13.200
Hello?

01:26:13.768 --> 01:26:16.068
Hello. Hi.

01:26:17.597 --> 01:26:19.371
I... How are you?

01:26:21.308 --> 01:26:22.868
I'm sorry, I should have called

01:26:23.003 --> 01:26:25.007
after the attack
at the White House.

01:26:25.143 --> 01:26:26.546
Are you okay?

01:26:26.681 --> 01:26:27.681
Oh...

01:26:28.178 --> 01:26:29.344
I'm fine.

01:26:29.746 --> 01:26:32.252
It's really good
to hear your voice.

01:26:34.088 --> 01:26:35.750
I didn't think you'd answer.

01:26:36.920 --> 01:26:41.624
Betty, I... I know I've
made a lot of mistakes.

01:26:42.926 --> 01:26:48.466
But I'm trying to change,
to be a better person.

01:26:49.770 --> 01:26:50.798
Um...

01:26:51.735 --> 01:26:56.237
Maybe we could take
a... a walk sometime?

01:26:56.873 --> 01:27:02.348
See the cherry blossoms,
like the old days.

01:27:05.746 --> 01:27:09.586
Yeah. That could be nice.

01:27:11.717 --> 01:27:15.053
Okay. I love you.

01:27:15.764 --> 01:27:17.088
Bye, Dad.

01:27:37.444 --> 01:27:38.549
Please.

01:27:39.384 --> 01:27:41.145
Good afternoon, everyone.

01:27:44.223 --> 01:27:45.623
When I took office,

01:27:45.758 --> 01:27:51.288
I promised we would create
a true, lasting peace.

01:27:52.125 --> 01:27:56.501
Today, we begin to
realize that promise.

01:27:57.897 --> 01:27:59.570
Captain America...

01:28:02.308 --> 01:28:03.740
would you do me the kindness

01:28:03.875 --> 01:28:07.904
of counseling a bitter man
at the end of his rope?

01:28:08.040 --> 01:28:10.042
That's what you do, isn't it?

01:28:11.053 --> 01:28:12.319
Guess we have five minutes

01:28:12.454 --> 01:28:14.212
until the MPs drag
your ass outta here.

01:28:14.347 --> 01:28:17.818
You ruined my grand finale
on the Indian Ocean.

01:28:17.953 --> 01:28:19.892
So now I'm forced
to turn myself in

01:28:20.028 --> 01:28:21.293
to get what I want.

01:28:21.429 --> 01:28:23.226
Well, if you're
waitin' for an apology,

01:28:23.361 --> 01:28:24.690
we'll be here awhile.

01:28:24.826 --> 01:28:26.397
I'm waiting for you to realize

01:28:26.532 --> 01:28:28.761
that we both want
the same thing,

01:28:29.130 --> 01:28:31.434
for the world to see
Ross as he truly is.

01:28:31.903 --> 01:28:36.843
I'm proud to say our treaty
will finally be signed.

01:28:37.212 --> 01:28:38.944
I'll take a couple questions.

01:28:39.380 --> 01:28:40.643
Sir, what do you say to reports

01:28:40.778 --> 01:28:42.640
that relations with
Japan broke down

01:28:42.775 --> 01:28:44.043
over your handling

01:28:44.178 --> 01:28:45.562
of the White House
assassination attempt?

01:28:45.586 --> 01:28:48.186
Despite fabrications
that some have used

01:28:48.322 --> 01:28:50.056
to turn us against each other,

01:28:50.192 --> 01:28:53.158
our bonds have proved strong.

01:28:53.294 --> 01:28:55.788
You kept Ross alive for years.

01:28:56.424 --> 01:28:59.432
Didn't kill him when you had
the chance at the White House.

01:29:00.595 --> 01:29:02.228
The way I see it,

01:29:03.164 --> 01:29:06.472
the Indian Ocean wasn't
about starting a war.

01:29:07.574 --> 01:29:09.640
You wanted to
destroy his legacy.

01:29:10.636 --> 01:29:12.005
Yes.

01:29:13.171 --> 01:29:14.913
But you haven't figured out how.

01:29:15.048 --> 01:29:16.412
The pills.

01:29:16.547 --> 01:29:18.275
I got somebody on that too.

01:29:18.878 --> 01:29:20.513
Not anymore, you don't.

01:29:21.182 --> 01:29:23.147
Is it true hostilities
in the Indian Ocean

01:29:23.282 --> 01:29:25.158
occurred because the
Japanese discovered

01:29:25.293 --> 01:29:26.655
it was, in fact, your government

01:29:26.791 --> 01:29:28.786
who paid for the
SERPENT mercenary group

01:29:28.922 --> 01:29:30.628
to steal their adamantium?

01:29:31.396 --> 01:29:32.989
We did not pay them.

01:29:33.125 --> 01:29:35.059
Ross turned me into a monster.

01:29:35.428 --> 01:29:38.504
It's only right that I
do the same thing to him.

01:29:39.305 --> 01:29:40.731
Why aren't you smiling?

01:29:41.100 --> 01:29:43.234
- On the ground!
- Hold it!

01:29:48.241 --> 01:29:49.680
You ever use that
big brain of yours

01:29:49.815 --> 01:29:53.211
to consider that maybe
you're wrong about Ross?

01:29:53.647 --> 01:29:54.647
Wanna bet?

01:29:54.714 --> 01:29:55.714
Yeah.

01:29:56.856 --> 01:29:59.250
- Where are you going?
- To stop this.

01:30:00.062 --> 01:30:01.725
Get on the ground, now.

01:30:03.125 --> 01:30:04.568
You have the right
to remain silent...

01:30:04.592 --> 01:30:05.758
Captain America!

01:30:06.227 --> 01:30:10.362
If I'm right about Ross,
you're going to die.

01:30:10.831 --> 01:30:12.396
You're going to die!

01:30:13.199 --> 01:30:15.832
Mr. President,
Dr. Samuel Sterns

01:30:15.968 --> 01:30:17.637
just turned himself in.

01:30:18.073 --> 01:30:19.810
He claims you
promised him a pardon

01:30:19.946 --> 01:30:22.612
if he worked on secret
government projects for you.

01:30:22.748 --> 01:30:24.253
That is a lie.

01:30:24.277 --> 01:30:25.942
President Ross,

01:30:26.078 --> 01:30:27.454
I miss our little visits.

01:30:27.589 --> 01:30:29.222
What do you want?

01:30:29.357 --> 01:30:30.818
I wanted
my life back,

01:30:30.954 --> 01:30:32.319
but it's too late for that now.

01:30:32.454 --> 01:30:33.559
Sir...

01:30:33.694 --> 01:30:34.831
I helped you
more than anyone else.

01:30:34.855 --> 01:30:36.061
Well, let me explain.

01:30:36.196 --> 01:30:37.397
They have to know.

01:30:37.532 --> 01:30:39.126
You gotta
understand my position.

01:30:39.261 --> 01:30:42.836
Oh, I do. You
let me rot in this prison.

01:30:42.971 --> 01:30:44.229
Leave me alone!

01:30:44.364 --> 01:30:46.137
- Leave me! Let me go!
- Sir! Sir!

01:30:46.272 --> 01:30:47.506
I cannot let you.

01:30:47.642 --> 01:30:49.543
- You can't let me? Let me?
- I cannot...

01:30:49.678 --> 01:30:53.413
Everyone will
know just who you are.

01:30:53.548 --> 01:30:55.849
And Betty will
despise you even more.

01:30:55.984 --> 01:30:57.642
Sir, please.

01:31:07.523 --> 01:31:08.594
Sir.

01:31:15.003 --> 01:31:16.529
Oh, my God.

01:31:37.391 --> 01:31:38.983
Since when were they red?

01:31:44.329 --> 01:31:45.723
President Ross?

01:31:49.161 --> 01:31:50.603
Agent Taylor, do we fire?

01:32:26.869 --> 01:32:28.707
This is what Sterns wanted.

01:32:38.613 --> 01:32:39.685
Jesus.

01:32:45.485 --> 01:32:47.124
Sam, I gotta get these
people outta here.

01:32:47.259 --> 01:32:48.599
Set a
perimeter around the White House.

01:33:17.083 --> 01:33:18.158
No.

01:33:18.293 --> 01:33:20.253
Fall back. Fall back!

01:33:26.860 --> 01:33:28.129
Get down!

01:33:30.504 --> 01:33:32.166
Sam, drones incoming.

01:34:16.752 --> 01:34:18.779
Ruth, I need you to
clear Hains Point.

01:34:18.914 --> 01:34:20.213
I'll lure Ross there.

01:34:20.349 --> 01:34:22.650
Sam, are you
crazy? He'll kill you.

01:34:22.786 --> 01:34:24.119
Do it!

01:35:20.980 --> 01:35:23.008
You can still fight this, Ross.

01:35:23.144 --> 01:35:25.015
Do you see where you are?

01:35:27.246 --> 01:35:28.811
You remember this place?

01:35:29.714 --> 01:35:32.022
You used to come
here with Betty.

01:35:35.055 --> 01:35:36.389
That didn't work.

01:35:44.997 --> 01:35:45.997
Okay.

01:35:46.065 --> 01:35:47.367
You want me?

01:35:48.573 --> 01:35:49.900
Come and get me!

01:37:38.249 --> 01:37:40.581
Sam? Sam,
can you hear me?

01:37:41.117 --> 01:37:42.614
Sam, are you okay?

01:37:49.294 --> 01:37:51.693
Please tell me I knocked
that son of a bitch out.

01:37:58.702 --> 01:37:59.730
Shit.

01:38:05.207 --> 01:38:06.636
Backup's five minutes away.

01:38:06.772 --> 01:38:08.874
No,
tell them wait.

01:38:09.009 --> 01:38:10.477
What?

01:38:19.991 --> 01:38:21.318
Should've taken that serum.

01:38:21.453 --> 01:38:23.461
Bucky is full of shit.

01:38:27.833 --> 01:38:29.430
I'm gonna lose that bet.

01:38:36.608 --> 01:38:37.802
Ross.

01:38:37.937 --> 01:38:40.612
We both know you can take
me out with one punch,

01:38:41.114 --> 01:38:43.114
but I don't think
you wanna do that.

01:38:50.454 --> 01:38:53.718
I know you've done
some terrible things.

01:38:55.421 --> 01:38:57.029
Now, I might be crazy...

01:38:58.032 --> 01:39:00.464
but I think you're
trying to change.

01:39:01.267 --> 01:39:03.497
Now's the time to
prove it to the world.

01:39:04.396 --> 01:39:05.798
Prove it to Betty.

01:40:00.855 --> 01:40:03.997
The army is transferring
Sterns to a secure facility.

01:40:05.132 --> 01:40:06.727
We should get you
to the hospital.

01:40:07.596 --> 01:40:10.036
There's somewhere
we gotta go first.

01:40:22.145 --> 01:40:23.709
That's three, old man.

01:40:25.776 --> 01:40:27.350
I told you I'd get you out.

01:40:28.117 --> 01:40:29.455
Took you so long?

01:40:33.825 --> 01:40:35.160
Thank you, Sam.

01:40:35.596 --> 01:40:36.596
I got you.

01:40:36.724 --> 01:40:38.757
I have a few broken bones, so...

01:40:42.297 --> 01:40:43.530
Come on, Mr. Bradley.

01:40:43.666 --> 01:40:45.771
We got a little
paperwork to fill out,

01:40:45.906 --> 01:40:47.997
and then you're free to go.

01:40:54.247 --> 01:40:55.847
Worldwide talks continue

01:40:55.877 --> 01:40:58.645
in the arms race for the
new discovered element

01:40:58.780 --> 01:41:02.111
as we enter the brave
new world of adamantium.

01:41:02.246 --> 01:41:04.386
Back in our nation's
capital, ground was broken

01:41:04.522 --> 01:41:06.487
on the restoration
of the White House,

01:41:06.623 --> 01:41:09.385
marking a significant
step towards normalcy

01:41:09.520 --> 01:41:10.520
for the country.

01:41:28.913 --> 01:41:30.182
Right this way.

01:41:38.026 --> 01:41:42.128
Mr. President.
How're your digs?

01:41:49.464 --> 01:41:51.632
Intentionally uncomfortable.

01:41:52.802 --> 01:41:54.974
I heard the food hasn't
got any better either.

01:41:55.109 --> 01:41:57.242
You heard right.

01:41:57.843 --> 01:41:58.973
Bradley got out?

01:41:59.108 --> 01:42:00.236
Yes, sir.

01:42:00.571 --> 01:42:01.705
That's good.

01:42:02.040 --> 01:42:03.974
Mr. President, about
your blood work.

01:42:04.109 --> 01:42:06.609
It seems Sterns raised
the level of gamma

01:42:06.745 --> 01:42:08.416
in those pills over time.

01:42:08.552 --> 01:42:11.085
It built up in your
body over the years.

01:42:11.221 --> 01:42:12.054
That led to your...

01:42:12.190 --> 01:42:13.858
Led to my little tantrum.

01:42:14.261 --> 01:42:16.492
Which is why I
have to be in here.

01:42:18.426 --> 01:42:20.631
Good solid walls, these.

01:42:20.766 --> 01:42:21.827
Yeah.

01:42:22.396 --> 01:42:23.734
But I have to say,

01:42:24.103 --> 01:42:25.269
it wasn't nothin' to see you

01:42:25.405 --> 01:42:28.137
take full responsibility
for your actions.

01:42:28.639 --> 01:42:32.736
Give up your office.
Accept your sentence.

01:42:32.871 --> 01:42:34.907
I had to let the
country move on.

01:42:35.877 --> 01:42:38.340
Japan decided to uphold
the treaty, by the way.

01:42:38.476 --> 01:42:39.476
Us too.

01:42:40.118 --> 01:42:42.419
The Ozaki-Ross Accords.

01:42:43.020 --> 01:42:44.280
You did it.

01:42:44.749 --> 01:42:46.489
Sam, why are you here?

01:42:47.552 --> 01:42:48.590
Sir?

01:42:50.298 --> 01:42:52.094
We were on different
sides of this thing

01:42:52.229 --> 01:42:53.694
every step of the way.

01:42:55.369 --> 01:42:57.500
Look, if we can't see
the good in each other,

01:42:58.567 --> 01:43:00.338
we've already lost the fight.

01:43:01.707 --> 01:43:05.310
Besides, I wanted to make
sure an old soldier was okay.

01:43:07.505 --> 01:43:11.316
I'd love to stay, but looks
like you have another visitor.

01:43:20.452 --> 01:43:21.623
Hi, Dad.

01:43:25.357 --> 01:43:29.026
I guess I have to give you
a raincheck on that walk.

01:43:30.133 --> 01:43:31.501
It's all right.

01:43:33.298 --> 01:43:35.769
We could just sit and
talk for a little while.

01:43:37.779 --> 01:43:39.168
I'd like that.

01:43:40.714 --> 01:43:42.072
Me too.

01:43:55.293 --> 01:43:56.626
How's the kid doin' today?

01:43:56.761 --> 01:44:00.123
He's still a little out
of it but doin' better.

01:44:01.126 --> 01:44:02.400
I'm gonna let you two catch up.

01:44:02.535 --> 01:44:04.765
Hey, where you headed?
Back to Baltimore?

01:44:05.167 --> 01:44:06.203
No.

01:44:06.839 --> 01:44:10.208
I got Ruth and me tickets for
tonight's game, courtside.

01:44:10.610 --> 01:44:12.673
It's the least I could
do for gettin' me out.

01:44:12.809 --> 01:44:14.379
You know, I'm happy
you found a friend

01:44:14.514 --> 01:44:16.645
as grumpy as you are
to go to games with.

01:44:18.919 --> 01:44:20.143
Say it again.

01:44:23.256 --> 01:44:26.083
I'm
playing. Got you.

01:44:31.856 --> 01:44:34.498
The Falcon awakens.

01:44:36.095 --> 01:44:37.600
Couldn't let you
have all the fun.

01:44:43.076 --> 01:44:45.043
I'm sorry I screwed up.

01:44:45.178 --> 01:44:46.975
Screwed up? Get out of here.

01:44:47.110 --> 01:44:48.276
I did.

01:44:48.679 --> 01:44:50.382
You never messed up like I have.

01:44:51.418 --> 01:44:53.175
You never got shot
out of the sky

01:44:53.310 --> 01:44:56.520
and nosedived into
the Indian Ocean.

01:44:57.255 --> 01:44:58.722
You're always on point.

01:45:00.794 --> 01:45:02.020
Yeah.

01:45:03.857 --> 01:45:05.760
Because if I'm not on point...

01:45:10.004 --> 01:45:11.460
I feel like I let down

01:45:11.596 --> 01:45:14.230
everyone else who was fightin'
for a seat at that table.

01:45:17.077 --> 01:45:19.037
That's pressure, man.

01:45:20.871 --> 01:45:22.447
It weighs on you.

01:45:25.442 --> 01:45:28.277
Makes you wonder if
you'll ever just be...

01:45:30.054 --> 01:45:31.489
enough.

01:45:40.725 --> 01:45:41.763
Where I grew up,

01:45:42.865 --> 01:45:45.504
I only ever got to
see heroes online.

01:45:45.873 --> 01:45:47.373
Or on TV.

01:45:48.802 --> 01:45:50.509
It always felt so far away.

01:45:51.579 --> 01:45:54.303
And I kept thinkin' maybe
if I get out of Miami,

01:45:55.406 --> 01:45:56.882
you know, maybe one
day I could be...

01:45:57.017 --> 01:45:58.683
Don't say Ant-Man.

01:46:02.014 --> 01:46:03.719
No, man.

01:46:07.787 --> 01:46:09.153
I wanted to be you.

01:46:10.556 --> 01:46:11.194
Well...

01:46:11.329 --> 01:46:12.796
Sam Wilson.

01:46:13.832 --> 01:46:18.294
Because that guy? That
guy won't ever give up.

01:46:20.132 --> 01:46:21.730
That pressure,
that responsibility

01:46:21.865 --> 01:46:22.938
you talk about?

01:46:23.440 --> 01:46:25.378
I want that too, man.

01:46:34.555 --> 01:46:36.548
You know it's all
about timin', right?

01:46:37.517 --> 01:46:42.351
Control your spin, then hit
your thruster before you kick.

01:46:46.530 --> 01:46:48.794
- No.
- Yeah.

01:46:48.929 --> 01:46:50.425
No. That's...

01:46:50.861 --> 01:46:51.936
That's it.

01:46:52.706 --> 01:46:54.631
I should get shot out
of the sky more often.

01:46:54.766 --> 01:46:55.933
Yeah, you will.

01:46:56.069 --> 01:46:58.173
Okay.

01:46:58.909 --> 01:47:01.337
You know, you're gonna
come back from this.

01:47:01.816 --> 01:47:02.816
I know.

01:47:03.950 --> 01:47:08.277
And when that time comes,
make sure the suit's ready,

01:47:08.413 --> 01:47:10.687
'cause Ross was right
about one thing.

01:47:11.457 --> 01:47:13.784
The world needs the Avengers.

01:47:13.920 --> 01:47:16.028
- For real?
- Yeah.

01:47:16.163 --> 01:47:18.024
Hell, yeah.

01:47:19.467 --> 01:47:20.674
I wasn't thinking
about it before,

01:47:20.698 --> 01:47:22.591
but now that you bring it up...

01:47:22.727 --> 01:47:23.830
Oh, boy.

01:47:23.965 --> 01:47:25.165
...since the
wings are damaged,

01:47:25.299 --> 01:47:26.817
I was thinking, I'm
like, what could make...

01:47:26.841 --> 01:47:27.841
No.

01:47:27.898 --> 01:47:29.400
You didn't hear

01:47:29.536 --> 01:47:31.016
- what I was gonna ask you.
- No. Whatever you ask, nope.

01:47:31.040 --> 01:47:32.936
I'm just saying,
maybe you have, like,

01:47:33.071 --> 01:47:34.573
the Wakandans on speed dial

01:47:34.709 --> 01:47:35.711
and could get me some...

01:47:35.846 --> 01:47:39.685
A hookup on an
upgrade on the wings.

01:47:40.688 --> 01:47:43.382
You're gonna ask the
Wakandans for a hookup?

01:47:43.517 --> 01:47:44.622
Yeah.

01:47:44.757 --> 01:47:46.397
That is the most Miami
thing in the world.

01:47:46.485 --> 01:47:48.584
Are you kidding? They
gonna hook me up, man. Yo.

01:57:19.494 --> 01:57:21.495
Told you you were
gonna lose that bet.

01:57:22.836 --> 01:57:24.199
You wanna know what's funny?

01:57:24.335 --> 01:57:27.028
I'm not in the mood
for your jokes.

01:57:27.397 --> 01:57:29.998
You killed a lot of good men
trying to get your revenge.

01:57:30.133 --> 01:57:32.974
Trust me, we don't share
the same sense of humor.

01:57:33.343 --> 01:57:35.875
We share the same
world, don't we?

01:57:36.545 --> 01:57:39.315
This world you
would die to save?

01:57:40.983 --> 01:57:42.147
It's coming.

01:57:42.716 --> 01:57:44.755
I've seen it in
the probabilities,

01:57:44.890 --> 01:57:46.818
seen it plain as day.

01:57:47.754 --> 01:57:50.789
All you heroes
protecting this world,

01:57:51.692 --> 01:57:53.725
do you think you're
the only ones?

01:57:54.662 --> 01:57:57.465
Do you think this
is the only world?

01:57:58.871 --> 01:58:00.272
We'll see what happens

01:58:00.407 --> 01:58:04.703
when you have to protect
this place from the others.
